      "content": [
        "Deuteronomy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc2",
      "content": [
        "Deuteronomy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc3",
      "content": [
        "DEU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "mt1",
      "content": [
        "Deuteronomy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "1",
      "sid": "DEU 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Command to Leave Horeb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 33:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 33:1–6"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 1:1"
        },
        "These are the words that Moses spoke to all Israel in the wilderness east of the Jordan — in the Arabah opposite Suph — between Paran and Tophel, Laban, Hazeroth, and Dizahab."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 1:2"
        },
        "It is an eleven-day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "journey"
          ]
        },
        " from Horeb",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai; also in verses 6 and 19"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to Kadesh-barnea by way of Mount Seir. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 1:3"
        },
        "In the fortieth year, on the first day of the eleventh month, Moses proclaimed to the Israelites all that the LORD had commanded him concerning them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 1:4"
        },
        "This was after he had defeated Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon, and then at Edrei ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had defeated"
          ]
        },
        " Og king of Bashan, who lived in Ashtaroth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 1:5"
        },
        "On the east side of the Jordan in the land of Moab, Moses began to explain this law, saying:",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Note that ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 1:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 1:6"
                  ]
                },
                " through Deuteronomy 4:40 may be presented as a continuous section of unbroken speech by Moses. In place of multiple levels of nested quotes, this section has been set apart with a double space."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 1:6"
        },
        "The LORD our God said to us at Horeb: “You have stayed at this mountain long enough. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 1:7"
        },
        "Resume your journey and go to the hill country of the Amorites; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "go"
          ]
        },
        " to all the neighboring peoples in the Arabah, in the hill country, in the foothills,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Shephelah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "lowlands"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; that is, the western foothills of Judea"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " in the Negev, and along the seacoast to the land of the Canaanites and to Lebanon, as far as the great River Euphrates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 1:8"
        },
        "See, I have placed the land before you. Enter and possess the land that the LORD swore He would give to your fathers Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and to their descendants after them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Moses Appoints Leaders"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 18:13-27",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 18:13–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 1:9"
        },
        "At that time I said to you, “I cannot carry the burden for you alone. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 1:10"
        },
        "The LORD your God has multiplied you, so that today you are as numerous as the stars in the sky. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 1:11"
        },
        "May the LORD, the God of your fathers, increase you a thousand times over and bless you as He has promised. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 1:12"
        },
        "But how can I bear your troubles, burdens, and disputes all by myself? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 1:13"
        },
        "Choose for yourselves wise, understanding, and respected men from each of your tribes, and I will appoint them as your leaders.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 1:14"
        },
        "And you answered me and said, “What you propose to do is good.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 1:15"
        },
        "So I took the leaders of your tribes, wise and respected men, and appointed them as leaders over you — as commanders of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens, and as officers for your tribes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 1:16"
        },
        "At that time I charged your judges: “Hear the disputes between your brothers, and judge fairly between a man and his brother or a foreign resident. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 1:17"
        },
        "Show no partiality in judging; hear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "both"
          ]
        },
        " small and great alike. Do not be intimidated by anyone, for judgment belongs to God. And bring to me any case too difficult for you, and I will hear it.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 1:18"
        },
        "And at that time I commanded you all the things you were to do."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Twelve Spies Sent Out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 13:1-33",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 13:1–33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 1:19"
        },
        "And just as the LORD our God had commanded us, we set out from Horeb and went toward the hill country of the Amorites, through all the vast and terrifying wilderness you have seen. When we reached Kadesh-barnea, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 1:20"
        },
        "I said: “You have reached the hill country of the Amorites, which the LORD our God is giving us. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 1:21"
        },
        "See, the LORD your God has placed the land before you. Go up and take possession of it as the LORD, the God of your fathers, has told you. Do not be afraid or discouraged.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 1:22"
        },
        "Then all of you approached me and said, “Let us send men ahead of us to search out the land and bring us word of what route to follow and which cities to enter.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 1:23"
        },
        "The plan seemed good to me, so I selected twelve men from among you, one from each tribe. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 1:24"
        },
        "They left and went up into the hill country, and came to the Valley of Eshcol and spied out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 1:25"
        },
        "They took some of the fruit of the land in their hands, carried it down to us, and brought us word: “It is a good land that the LORD our God is giving us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Israel’s Rebellion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 14:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 14:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 1:26"
        },
        "But you were unwilling to go up; you rebelled against the command of the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 1:27"
        },
        "You grumbled in your tents and said, “Because the LORD hates us, He has brought us out of the land of Egypt to deliver us into the hand of the Amorites to be annihilated. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 1:28"
        },
        "Where can we go? Our brothers have made our hearts melt, saying: ‘The people are larger and taller than we are; the cities are large, with walls up to the heavens. We even saw the descendants of the Anakim there.’”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 1:29"
        },
        "So I said to you: “Do not be terrified or afraid of them! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 1:30"
        },
        "The LORD your God, who goes before you, will fight for you, just as you saw Him do for you in Egypt ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 1:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " in the wilderness, where the LORD your God carried you, as a man carries his son, all the way by which you traveled until you reached this place.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 1:32"
        },
        "But in spite of all this, you did not trust the LORD your God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "DEU 1:33"
        },
        "who went before you on the journey, in the fire by night and in the cloud by day, to seek out a place for you to camp ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " to show you the road to travel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Israel’s Penalty"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 14:20-35",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 14:20–35"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "DEU 1:34"
        },
        "When the LORD heard your words, He grew angry and swore an oath, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "DEU 1:35"
        },
        "“Not one of the men of this evil generation shall see the good land I swore to give your fathers, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "DEU 1:36"
        },
        "except Caleb son of Jephunneh. He will see it, and I will give him and his descendants the land on which he has set foot, because he followed the LORD wholeheartedly.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "DEU 1:37"
        },
        "The LORD was also angry with me on your account, and He said, “Not even you shall enter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "DEU 1:38"
        },
        "Joshua son of Nun, who stands before you, will enter it. Encourage him, for he will enable Israel to inherit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "DEU 1:39"
        },
        "And the little ones you said would become captives — your children who on that day did not know good from evil — will enter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land that"
          ]
        },
        " I will give them, and they will possess it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "DEU 1:40"
        },
        "But you are to turn back and head for the wilderness along the route to the Red Sea.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:40 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Sea of Reeds"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Defeat at Hormah"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 14:40-45",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 14:40–45"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "DEU 1:41"
        },
        "“We have sinned against the LORD,” you replied. “We will go up and fight, as the LORD our God has commanded us.” Then each of you put on his weapons of war, thinking it easy to go up into the hill country."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "DEU 1:42"
        },
        "But the LORD said to me, “Tell them not to go up and fight, for I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "am"
          ]
        },
        " not with you to keep you from defeat by your enemies.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "DEU 1:43"
        },
        "So I spoke to you, but you would not listen. You rebelled against the command of the LORD and presumptuously went up into the hill country."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "DEU 1:44"
        },
        "Then the Amorites who lived in the hills came out against you and chased you like a swarm of bees. They routed you from Seir all the way to Hormah. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "DEU 1:45"
        },
        "And you returned and wept before the LORD, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " would not listen to your voice ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " give ear to you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "DEU 1:46"
        },
        "For this reason you stayed in Kadesh for a long time — a very long time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "2",
      "sid": "DEU 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Wanderings in the Wilderness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 2:1"
        },
        "Then we turned back and headed for the wilderness by way of the Red Sea,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Sea of Reeds"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " as the LORD had instructed me, and for many days we wandered around Mount Seir."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 2:2"
        },
        "At this time the LORD said to me, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 2:3"
        },
        "“You have been wandering around this hill country long enough; turn to the north ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 2:4"
        },
        "and command the people: ‘You will pass through the territory of your brothers, the descendants of Esau, who live in Seir. They will be afraid of you, so you must be very careful. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 2:5"
        },
        "Do not provoke them, for I will not give you any of their land, not even a footprint, because I have given Mount Seir to Esau as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " possession. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 2:6"
        },
        "You are to pay them in silver for the food you eat and the water you drink.’”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 2:7"
        },
        "Indeed, the LORD your God has blessed you in all the work of your hands. He has watched over your journey through this vast wilderness. The LORD your God has been with you these forty years, and you have lacked nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 2:8"
        },
        "So we passed by our brothers, the descendants of Esau, who live in Seir. We turned away from the Arabah road, which comes up from Elath and Ezion-geber, and traveled along the road of the Wilderness of Moab. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 2:9"
        },
        "Then the LORD said to me, “Do not harass the Moabites ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " provoke them to war, for I will not give you any of their land, because I have given Ar to the descendants of Lot as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " possession.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 2:10"
        },
        "(The Emites used to live there, a people great and many, as tall as the Anakites. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 2:11"
        },
        "Like the Anakites, they were also regarded as Rephaim, though the Moabites called them Emites. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 2:12"
        },
        "The Horites used to live in Seir, but the descendants of Esau drove them out. They destroyed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Horites"
          ]
        },
        " from before them and settled in their place, just as Israel did in the land that the LORD gave them as their possession.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 2:13"
        },
        "“Now arise and cross over the Brook of Zered.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "So we crossed over the Brook of Zered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 2:14"
        },
        "The time we spent traveling from Kadesh-barnea until we crossed over the Brook of Zered was thirty-eight years, until that entire generation of fighting men had perished from the camp, as the LORD had sworn to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 2:15"
        },
        "Indeed, the LORD’s hand was against them, to eliminate them from the camp, until they had all perished."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 2:16"
        },
        "Now when all the fighting men among the people had died, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 2:17"
        },
        "the LORD said to me, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 2:18"
        },
        "“Today you are going to cross the border of Moab at Ar. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 2:19"
        },
        "But when you get close to the Ammonites, do not harass them or provoke them, for I will not give you any of the land of the Ammonites. I have given it to the descendants of Lot as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " possession.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 2:20"
        },
        "(That too was regarded as the land of the Rephaim, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " used to live there, though the Ammonites called them Zamzummites. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 2:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They were"
          ]
        },
        " a people great and many, as tall as the Anakites. But the LORD destroyed them from before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Ammonites"
          ]
        },
        ", who drove them out and settled in their place, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 2:22"
        },
        "just as He had done for the descendants of Esau who lived in Seir, when He destroyed the Horites from before them. They drove them out and have lived in their place to this day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 2:23"
        },
        "And the Avvim, who lived in villages as far as Gaza, were destroyed by the Caphtorites, who came out of Caphtor",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Crete"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and settled in their place.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Defeat of Sihon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 21:21-30",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 21:21–30"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 2:24"
        },
        "“Arise, set out, and cross the Arnon Valley. See, I have delivered into your hand Sihon the Amorite, king of Heshbon, and his land. Begin to take possession of it and engage him in battle. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 2:25"
        },
        "This very day I will begin to put the dread and fear of you upon all the nations under heaven. They will hear the reports of you and tremble in anguish because of you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 2:26"
        },
        "So from the Wilderness of Kedemoth I sent messengers with an offer of peace to Sihon king of Heshbon, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 2:27"
        },
        "“Let us pass through your land; we will stay on the main road. We will not turn to the right or to the left. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 2:28"
        },
        "You can sell us food to eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " water to drink in exchange for silver. Only let us pass through on foot, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 2:29"
        },
        "just as the descendants of Esau who live in Seir and the Moabites who live in Ar did for us, until we cross the Jordan into the land that the LORD our God is giving us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 2:30"
        },
        "But Sihon king of Heshbon would not let us pass through, for the LORD your God had made his spirit stubborn and his heart obstinate, that He might deliver him into your hand, as is the case this day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 2:31"
        },
        "Then the LORD said to me, “See, I have begun to deliver Sihon and his land over to you. Now begin to conquer and possess his land.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 2:32"
        },
        "So Sihon and his whole army came out for battle against us at Jahaz. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "DEU 2:33"
        },
        "And the LORD our God delivered him over to us, and we defeated him and his sons and his whole army."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "DEU 2:34"
        },
        "At that time we captured all his cities and devoted to destruction",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:34 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "cherem "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " the people of every city, including women and children. We left no survivors. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "DEU 2:35"
        },
        "We carried off for ourselves only the livestock and the plunder from the cities we captured."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "DEU 2:36"
        },
        "From Aroer on the rim of the Arnon Valley, along with the city in the valley, even as far as Gilead, not one city ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had walls"
          ]
        },
        " too high for us. The LORD our God gave us all of them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "DEU 2:37"
        },
        "But you did not go near the land of the Ammonites, or ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        " along the banks of the Jabbok River, or the cities of the hill country, or any place that the LORD our God had forbidden."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "3",
      "sid": "DEU 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Defeat of Og"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 21:31-35",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 21:31–35"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 3:1"
        },
        "Then we turned and went up the road to Bashan, and Og king of Bashan and his whole army came out to meet us in battle at Edrei. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 3:2"
        },
        "But the LORD said to me, “Do not fear him, for I have delivered him into your hand, along with all his people and his land. Do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 3:3"
        },
        "So the LORD our God also delivered Og king of Bashan and his whole army into our hands. We struck them down until no survivor was left."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 3:4"
        },
        "At that time we captured all sixty of his cities. There was not a single city we failed to take — the entire region of Argob, the kingdom of Og in Bashan. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 3:5"
        },
        "All these cities were fortified with high walls and gates and bars, and there were many more unwalled villages. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 3:6"
        },
        "We devoted them to destruction,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "cherem "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " as we had done to Sihon king of Heshbon, utterly destroying the men, women, and children of every city."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 3:7"
        },
        "But all the livestock and plunder of the cities we carried off for ourselves."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 3:8"
        },
        "At that time we took from the two kings of the Amorites the land across the Jordan, from the Arnon Valley as far as Mount Hermon — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 3:9"
        },
        "which the Sidonians call Sirion but the Amorites call Senir — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 3:10"
        },
        "all the cities of the plateau, all of Gilead, and all of Bashan as far as the cities of Salecah and Edrei in the kingdom of Og."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 3:11"
        },
        "(For only Og king of Bashan had remained of the remnant of the Rephaim. His bed of iron, nine cubits long and four cubits wide,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Og’s bed was approximately 14 feet long and 6 feet wide (4.3 meters long and 1.8 meters wide)."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is still"
          ]
        },
        " in Rabbah of the Ammonites.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Land Division East of the Jordan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 32:1-42",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 32:1–42"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOS 13:8-14",
          "content": [
            "Joshua 13:8–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 3:12"
        },
        "So at that time we took possession of this land. To the Reubenites and Gadites I gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        " beyond Aroer along the Arnon Valley, and half the hill country of Gilead, along with its cities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 3:13"
        },
        "To the half-tribe of Manasseh I gave the rest of Gilead and all of Bashan, the kingdom of Og. (The entire region of Argob, the whole territory of Bashan, used to be called the land of the Rephaim.) ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 3:14"
        },
        "Jair, a descendant of Manasseh, took the whole region of Argob as far as the border of the Geshurites and Maacathites. He renamed Bashan after himself, Havvoth-jair,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the villages of Jair"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " by which ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is called"
          ]
        },
        " to this day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 3:15"
        },
        "To Machir I gave Gilead, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 3:16"
        },
        "and to the Reubenites and Gadites I gave the territory from Gilead to the Arnon Valley (the middle of the valley was the border) and up to the Jabbok River, the border of the Ammonites. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 3:17"
        },
        "The Jordan ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "River"
          ]
        },
        " in the Arabah bordered it from Chinnereth to the Sea of the Arabah (the Salt Sea",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the Dead Sea"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        ") with the slopes of Pisgah to the east."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 3:18"
        },
        "At that time I commanded you: “The LORD your God has given you this land to possess. All ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " men of valor are to cross over, armed for battle, ahead of your brothers, the Israelites. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 3:19"
        },
        "But your wives, your children, and your livestock— I know that you have much livestock— may remain in the cities I have given you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 3:20"
        },
        "until the LORD gives rest to your brothers as He has to you, and they too have taken possession of the land that the LORD your God is giving them across the Jordan. Then each of you may return to the possession I have given you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 3:21"
        },
        "And at that time I commanded Joshua: “Your own eyes have seen all that the LORD your God has done to these two kings. The LORD will do the same to all the kingdoms you are about to enter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 3:22"
        },
        "Do not be afraid of them, for the LORD your God Himself will fight for you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Moses Forbidden to Cross the Jordan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 27:12-17",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 27:12–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 3:23"
        },
        "At that time I also pleaded with the LORD: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 3:24"
        },
        "“O Lord GOD, You have begun to show Your greatness and power to Your servant. For what god in heaven or on earth can perform such works and mighty acts ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as Yours"
          ]
        },
        "? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 3:25"
        },
        "Please let me cross over and see the good land beyond the Jordan — that pleasant hill country as well as Lebanon!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 3:26"
        },
        "But the LORD was angry with me on account of you, and He would not listen to me. “That is enough,” the LORD said to me. “Do not speak to Me again about this matter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 3:27"
        },
        "Go to the top of Pisgah and look to the west and north and south and east. See ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        " with your own eyes, for you will not cross this Jordan. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 3:28"
        },
        "But commission Joshua, encourage him, and strengthen him, for he will cross over ahead of the people and enable them to inherit the land that you will see.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 3:29"
        },
        "So we stayed in the valley opposite Beth-peor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "4",
      "sid": "DEU 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "An Exhortation to Obedience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 11:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 11:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 4:1"
        },
        "Hear now, O Israel, the statutes and ordinances I am teaching you to follow, so that you may live and may enter and take possession of the land that the LORD, the God of your fathers, is giving you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 4:2"
        },
        "You must not add to or subtract from what I command you, so that you may keep the commandments of the LORD your God that I am giving you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 4:3"
        },
        "Your eyes have seen what the LORD did at Baal-peor, for the LORD your God destroyed from among you all who followed Baal of Peor. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 4:4"
        },
        "But you who held fast to the LORD your God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " alive to this day, every one of you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 4:5"
        },
        "See, I have taught you statutes and ordinances just as the LORD my God has commanded me, so that you may follow them in the land that you are about to enter and possess. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 4:6"
        },
        "Observe them carefully, for this will show your wisdom and understanding in the sight of the peoples, who will hear of all these statutes and say, “Surely this great nation ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a wise and understanding people.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 4:7"
        },
        "For what nation ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " great enough to have a god ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " near to them as the LORD our God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is to us"
          ]
        },
        " whenever we call on Him? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 4:8"
        },
        "And what nation ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " great enough to have righteous statutes and ordinances like this entire law I set before you today?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 4:9"
        },
        "Only be on your guard and diligently watch yourselves, so that you do not forget the things your eyes have seen, and so that they do not slip from your heart as long as you live. Teach them to your children and grandchildren. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 4:10"
        },
        "The day you stood before the LORD your God at Horeb,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai; also in verse 15"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " the LORD said to me, “Gather the people before Me to hear My words, so that they may learn to fear Me all the days they live on the earth, and that they may teach them to their children.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 4:11"
        },
        "You came near and stood at the base of the mountain, a mountain blazing with fire to the heavens, with black clouds and deep darkness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 4:12"
        },
        "And the LORD spoke to you out of the fire. You heard the sound of the words but saw no form; there was only a voice. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 4:13"
        },
        "He declared to you His covenant, which He commanded you to follow — the Ten Commandments",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Ten Words"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " that He wrote on two tablets of stone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 4:14"
        },
        "At that time the LORD commanded me to teach you the statutes and ordinances you are to follow in the land that you are crossing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Jordan"
          ]
        },
        " to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Warning against Idolatry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 12:29-32",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 12:29–32"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EZK 6:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Ezekiel 6:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 4:15"
        },
        "So since you saw no form of any kind on the day the LORD spoke to you out of the fire at Horeb, be careful ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 4:16"
        },
        "that you do not act corruptly and make an idol for yourselves of any form or shape, whether in the likeness of a male or female, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 4:17"
        },
        "of any beast that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " on the earth or bird that flies in the air, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 4:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " of any creature that crawls on the ground or fish that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " in the waters below."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 4:19"
        },
        "When you look to the heavens and see the sun and moon and stars— all the host of heaven— do not be enticed to bow down and worship what the LORD your God has apportioned to all the nations under heaven. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 4:20"
        },
        "Yet the LORD has taken you and brought you out of the iron furnace, out of Egypt, to be the people of His inheritance, as you are today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 4:21"
        },
        "The LORD, however, was angry with me on account of you, and He swore that I would not cross the Jordan to enter the good land that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 4:22"
        },
        "For I will not be crossing the Jordan, because I must die in this land. But you shall cross over and take possession of that good land."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 4:23"
        },
        "Be careful that you do not forget the covenant of the LORD your God that He made with you; do not make an idol for yourselves in the form of anything He has forbidden you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 4:24"
        },
        "For the LORD your God is a consuming fire,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 12:29",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 12:29"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " a jealous God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 4:25"
        },
        "After you have children and grandchildren and you have been in the land a long time, if you then act corruptly and make an idol of any form— doing evil in the sight of the LORD your God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " provoking Him to anger— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 4:26"
        },
        "I call heaven and earth as witnesses against you this day that you will quickly perish from the land that you are crossing the Jordan to possess. You will not live long upon it, but will be utterly destroyed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 4:27"
        },
        "Then the LORD will scatter you among the peoples, and only a few of you will survive among the nations to which the LORD will drive you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 4:28"
        },
        "And there you will serve man-made gods of wood and stone, which cannot see ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " hear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " smell."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 4:29"
        },
        "But if from there you will seek the LORD your God, you will find Him if you seek Him with all your heart and with all your soul. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 4:30"
        },
        "When you are in distress and all these things have happened to you, then in later days you will return to the LORD your God and listen to His voice. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 4:31"
        },
        "For the LORD your God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a merciful God; He will not abandon you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " destroy you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " forget the covenant with your fathers, which He swore to them by oath."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The LORD Alone Is God"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 4:32"
        },
        "Indeed, ask now from one end of the heavens to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the other"
          ]
        },
        " about the days that long preceded you, from the day that God created man on earth: Has anything as great as this ever happened or been reported? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "DEU 4:33"
        },
        "Has a people ever heard the voice of God",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of a god"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " speaking out of the fire, as you have, and lived? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "DEU 4:34"
        },
        "Or has any god tried to take as his own a nation out of another nation — by trials, signs, wonders, and war, by a strong hand and an outstretched arm, and by great terrors — as the LORD your God did for you in Egypt, before your eyes?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "DEU 4:35"
        },
        "You were shown ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these things"
          ]
        },
        " so that you would know that the LORD is God; there is no other besides Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "DEU 4:36"
        },
        "He let you hear His voice from heaven to discipline you, and on earth He showed you His great fire, and you heard His words out of the fire. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "DEU 4:37"
        },
        "Because He loved your fathers, He chose their descendants after them and brought you out of Egypt by His presence and great power, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "DEU 4:38"
        },
        "to drive out before you nations greater and mightier ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "than you"
          ]
        },
        ", and to bring you into their land and give it to you for your inheritance, as it is this day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "DEU 4:39"
        },
        "Know therefore this day and take to heart that the LORD is God in heaven above and on the earth below; there is no other. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "DEU 4:40"
        },
        "Keep His statutes and commandments, which I am giving you today, so that you and your children after you may prosper, and that you may live long in the land that the LORD your God is giving you for all time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Cities of Refuge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 35:9-34",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 35:9–34"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 19:1-14",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 19:1–14"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOS 20:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Joshua 20:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "DEU 4:41"
        },
        "Then Moses set aside three cities across the Jordan to the east ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "DEU 4:42"
        },
        "to which a manslayer could flee after killing his neighbor unintentionally without prior malice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "To save one’s own life, he could flee to one of these cities: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "DEU 4:43"
        },
        "Bezer in the wilderness on the plateau belonging to the Reubenites, Ramoth in Gilead belonging to the Gadites, or Golan in Bashan belonging to the Manassites."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Introduction to the Law"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "DEU 4:44"
        },
        "This is the law that Moses set before the Israelites. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "DEU 4:45"
        },
        "These ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " the testimonies, statutes, and ordinances that Moses proclaimed to them after they had come out of Egypt, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "DEU 4:46"
        },
        "while they were in the valley across the Jordan facing Beth-peor in the land of Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon and was defeated by Moses and the Israelites after they had come out of Egypt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "DEU 4:47"
        },
        "They took possession of the land ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "belonging to Sihon"
          ]
        },
        " and to Og king of Bashan — the two Amorite kings across the Jordan to the east — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "DEU 4:48"
        },
        "extending from Aroer on the rim of the Arnon Valley as far as Mount Siyon",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:48 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Sion"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Syriac "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Sirion"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " (that is, Hermon), ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "DEU 4:49"
        },
        "including all the Arabah on the east side of the Jordan and as far as the Sea of the Arabah,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:49 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the Dead Sea"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " below the slopes of Pisgah."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "5",
      "sid": "DEU 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Covenant at Horeb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 5:1"
        },
        "Then Moses summoned all Israel and said to them:",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Note that ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 5:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 5:1"
                  ]
                },
                " through Deuteronomy 26:19 may be presented as a continuous section of unbroken speech by Moses. In place of multiple levels of nested quotes, this section has been set apart with a double space."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Hear, O Israel, the statutes and ordinances that I declare in your hearing this day. Learn them and observe them carefully. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 5:2"
        },
        "The LORD our God made a covenant with us at Horeb.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 5:3"
        },
        "He did not make this covenant with our fathers, but with all of us who are alive here today. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 5:4"
        },
        "The LORD spoke with you face to face out of the fire on the mountain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Ten Commandments"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 20:1-17",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 20:1–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 5:5"
        },
        "At that time I was standing between the LORD and you to declare to you the word of the LORD, because you were afraid of the fire and would not go up the mountain. And He said: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 5:6"
        },
        "“I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 5:7"
        },
        "You shall have no other gods before Me.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "besides Me"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 5:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You shall"
          ]
        },
        " not make for yourself an idol in the form of anything in the heavens above, on the earth below, or in the waters beneath. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 5:9"
        },
        "You shall not bow down to them or worship them; for I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers on their children to the third and fourth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "generations"
          ]
        },
        " of those who hate Me, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 5:10"
        },
        "but showing loving devotion to a thousand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "generations"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "loving devotion to thousands"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "chesed "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "loving devotion"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; the range of meaning includes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "love"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "goodness"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "kindness"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "faithfulness"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", and "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "mercy"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", as well as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "loyalty to a covenant"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of those who love Me and keep My commandments."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 5:11"
        },
        "You shall not take the name of the LORD your God in vain, for the LORD will not leave anyone unpunished who takes His name in vain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 5:12"
        },
        "Observe the Sabbath day by keeping it holy, as the LORD your God has commanded you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 5:13"
        },
        "Six days you shall labor and do all your work, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 5:14"
        },
        "but the seventh day is a Sabbath to the LORD your God, on which you must not do any work— neither you, nor your son ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " daughter, nor your manservant ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " maidservant, nor your ox or donkey or any of your livestock, nor the foreigner within your gates, so that your manservant and maidservant may rest as you do. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 5:15"
        },
        "Remember that you were a slave in the land of Egypt, and that the LORD your God brought you out of there with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm. That is why the LORD your God has commanded you to keep the Sabbath day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 5:16"
        },
        "Honor your father and your mother, as the LORD your God has commanded you, so that your days may be long and that it may go well with you in the land that the LORD your God is giving you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 15:4",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 15:4"
                  ]
                },
                ", Matthew 19:19, Mark 7:10, Luke 18:20, and Ephesians 6:2–3"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 5:17"
        },
        "You shall not murder.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 5:21",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 5:21"
                  ]
                },
                ", Matthew 19:18, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, Romans 13:9, and James 2:11"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 5:18"
        },
        "You shall not commit adultery.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 5:27",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 5:27"
                  ]
                },
                ", Matthew 19:18, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, Romans 13:9, and James 2:11"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 5:19"
        },
        "You shall not steal.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 19:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 19:18"
                  ]
                },
                ", Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, and Romans 13:9"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 5:20"
        },
        "You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 19:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 19:18"
                  ]
                },
                ", Mark 10:19, and Luke 18:20"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 5:21"
        },
        "You shall not covet",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 7:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 7:7"
                  ]
                },
                " and Romans 13:9"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " your neighbor’s wife. You shall not covet your neighbor’s house or field, or his manservant or maidservant, or his ox or donkey, or anything that belongs to your neighbor.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Moses Intercedes for the People"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 20:18-21",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 20:18–21"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "HEB 12:18-29",
          "content": [
            "Hebrews 12:18–29"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 5:22"
        },
        "The LORD spoke these commandments in a loud voice to your whole assembly out of the fire, the cloud, and the deep darkness on the mountain; He added nothing more. And He wrote them on two tablets of stone and gave them to me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 5:23"
        },
        "And when you heard the voice out of the darkness while the mountain was blazing with fire, all the heads of your tribes and your elders approached me, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 5:24"
        },
        "and you said, “Behold, the LORD our God has shown us His glory and greatness, and we have heard His voice out of the fire. Today we have seen that a man can live ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even if"
          ]
        },
        " God speaks with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 5:25"
        },
        "But now, why should we die? For this great fire will consume us, and we will die, if we hear the voice of the LORD our God any longer. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 5:26"
        },
        "For who of all flesh has heard the voice of the living God speaking out of the fire, as we ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "have"
          ]
        },
        ", and survived? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 5:27"
        },
        "Go near and listen to all that the LORD our God says. Then you can tell us everything the LORD our God tells you; we will listen and obey.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 5:28"
        },
        "And the LORD heard the words you spoke to me, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " said to me, “I have heard the words that these people have spoken to you. They have done well in all that they have spoken. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 5:29"
        },
        "If only they had such a heart to fear Me and keep all My commandments always, so that it might be well with them and with their children forever. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 5:30"
        },
        "Go and tell them: ‘Return to your tents.’ ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 5:31"
        },
        "But you stand here with Me, that I may speak to you all the commandments and statutes and ordinances you are to teach them to follow in the land that I am giving them to possess.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 5:32"
        },
        "So be careful to do as the LORD your God has commanded you; you are not to turn aside to the right or to the left. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "DEU 5:33"
        },
        "You must walk in all the ways that the LORD your God has commanded you, so that you may live and prosper and prolong ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " days in the land that you will possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "6",
      "sid": "DEU 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Greatest Commandment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 22:34-40",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 22:34–40"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:28-34",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:28–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 6:1"
        },
        "These are the commandments and statutes and ordinances that the LORD your God has instructed me to teach you to follow in the land that you are about to enter and possess, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 6:2"
        },
        "so that you and your children and grandchildren may fear the LORD your God all the days of your lives by keeping all His statutes and commandments that I give you, and so that your days may be prolonged. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 6:3"
        },
        "Hear, O Israel, and be careful to observe them, so that you may prosper and multiply greatly in a land flowing with milk and honey, just as the LORD, the God of your fathers, has promised you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 6:4"
        },
        "Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God, the LORD is One.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "The LORD our God is One LORD "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "The LORD is our God, the LORD is One "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "The LORD is our God, the LORD alone"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MRK 12:29",
                  "content": [
                    "Mark 12:29"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 6:5"
        },
        "And you shall love the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your strength.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 22:37",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 22:37"
                  ]
                },
                ", Mark 12:30, and Luke 10:27"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 6:6"
        },
        "These words I am commanding you today are to be upon your hearts. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 6:7"
        },
        "And you shall teach them diligently to your children and speak of them when you sit at home and when you walk along the road, when you lie down and when you get up. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 6:8"
        },
        "Tie them as reminders on your hands and bind them on your foreheads. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 6:9"
        },
        "Write them on the doorposts of your houses and on your gates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 6:10"
        },
        "And when the LORD your God brings you into the land He swore to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, that He would give you— ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a land with"
          ]
        },
        " great and splendid cities that you did not build, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 6:11"
        },
        "with houses full of every good thing with which you did not fill them, with wells that you did not dig, and with vineyards and olive groves that you did not plant— and when you eat and are satisfied, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 6:12"
        },
        "be careful not to forget the LORD who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 6:13"
        },
        "Fear the LORD your God, serve Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "only"
          ]
        },
        ", and take your oaths in His name.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "serve Him, and take your oaths only in His name"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 4:10",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 4:10"
                  ]
                },
                " and Luke 4:8"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 6:14"
        },
        "Do not follow other gods, the gods of the peoples around you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 6:15"
        },
        "For the LORD your God, who is among you, is a jealous God. Otherwise the anger of the LORD your God will be kindled against you, and He will wipe you off the face of the earth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 6:16"
        },
        "Do not test the LORD your God as you tested Him at Massah.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Massah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "testing"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 17:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 17:7"
                  ]
                },
                "; cited in Matthew 4:7 and Luke 4:12."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 6:17"
        },
        "You are to diligently keep the commandments of the LORD your God and the testimonies and statutes He has given you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 6:18"
        },
        "Do what is right and good in the sight of the LORD, so that it may be well with you and that you may enter and possess the good land that the LORD your God swore to give your fathers, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 6:19"
        },
        "driving out all your enemies before you, as the LORD has said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Teach Your Children"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 6:20"
        },
        "In the future, when your son asks, “What is the meaning of the decrees and statutes and ordinances that the LORD our God has commanded you?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 6:21"
        },
        "then you are to tell him, “We were slaves of Pharaoh in Egypt, but the LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 6:22"
        },
        "Before our eyes the LORD inflicted great and devastating signs and wonders on Egypt, on Pharaoh, and on all his household. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 6:23"
        },
        "But He brought us out from there to lead us in and give us the land that He had sworn to our fathers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 6:24"
        },
        "And the LORD commanded us to observe all these statutes and to fear the LORD our God, that we may always be prosperous and preserved, as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we are"
          ]
        },
        " to this day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 6:25"
        },
        "And if we are careful to observe every one of these commandments before the LORD our God, as He has commanded us, then that will be our righteousness.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "7",
      "sid": "DEU 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Drive Out the Nations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 7:1"
        },
        "When the LORD your God brings you into the land that you are entering to possess, and He drives out before you many nations— the Hittites, Girgashites, Amorites, Canaanites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites, seven nations larger and stronger than you— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 7:2"
        },
        "and when the LORD your God has delivered them over to you to defeat them, then you must devote them to complete destruction.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "cherem "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also twice in verse 26."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Make no treaty",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "berit "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "are translated in most passages as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "covenant"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " with them and show them no mercy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 7:3"
        },
        "Do not intermarry with them. Do not give your daughters to their sons or take their daughters for your sons, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 7:4"
        },
        "because they will turn your sons away from following Me to serve other gods. Then the anger of the LORD will burn against you, and He will swiftly destroy you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 7:5"
        },
        "Instead, this is what you are to do to them: tear down their altars, smash their sacred pillars, cut down their Asherah poles, and burn their idols in the fire. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 7:6"
        },
        "For you are a people holy to the LORD your God. The LORD your God has chosen you to be a people for His prized possession out of all peoples on the face of the earth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 7:7"
        },
        "The LORD did not set His affection on you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " choose you because you were more numerous than the other peoples, for you were the fewest of all peoples. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 7:8"
        },
        "But because the LORD loved you and kept the oath He swore to your fathers, He brought you out with a mighty hand and redeemed you from the house of slavery, from the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 7:9"
        },
        "Know therefore that the LORD your God is God, the faithful God who keeps His covenant of loving devotion for a thousand generations of those who love Him and keep His commandments. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 7:10"
        },
        "But those who hate Him He repays to their faces with destruction; He will not hesitate to repay to his face the one who hates Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 7:11"
        },
        "So keep the commandments and statutes and ordinances that I am giving you to follow this day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Promises of God"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 23:20-33",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 23:20–33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 7:12"
        },
        "If you listen to these ordinances and keep them carefully, then the LORD your God will keep His covenant and the loving devotion that He swore to your fathers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 7:13"
        },
        "He will love you and bless you and multiply you. He will bless the fruit of your womb and the produce of your land— your grain, new wine, and oil, the young of your herds and the lambs of your flocks— in the land that He swore to your fathers to give you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 7:14"
        },
        "You will be blessed above all peoples; among you there will be no barren man or woman or livestock."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 7:15"
        },
        "And the LORD will remove from you all sickness. He will not lay upon you any of the terrible diseases you knew in Egypt, but He will inflict them on all who hate you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 7:16"
        },
        "You must destroy all the peoples the LORD your God will deliver to you. Do not look on them with pity. Do not worship their gods, for that will be a snare to you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 7:17"
        },
        "You may say in your heart, “These nations are greater than we are; how can we drive them out?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 7:18"
        },
        "But do not be afraid of them. Be sure to remember what the LORD your God did to Pharaoh and all Egypt: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 7:19"
        },
        "the great trials that you saw, the signs and wonders, and the mighty hand and outstretched arm by which the LORD your God brought you out. The LORD your God will do the same to all the peoples you now fear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 7:20"
        },
        "Moreover, the LORD your God will send the hornet against them until even the survivors hiding from you have perished. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 7:21"
        },
        "Do not be terrified by them, for the LORD your God, who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " among you, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a great and awesome God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 7:22"
        },
        "The LORD your God will drive out these nations before you little by little. You will not be enabled to eliminate them all at once, or the wild animals would multiply around you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 7:23"
        },
        "But the LORD your God will give them over to you and throw them into great confusion, until they are destroyed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 7:24"
        },
        "He will hand their kings over to you, and you will wipe out their names from under heaven. No one will be able to stand against you; you will annihilate them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 7:25"
        },
        "You must burn up the images of their gods; do not covet the silver and gold ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that is"
          ]
        },
        " on them or take it for yourselves, or you will be ensnared by it; for it is detestable to the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 7:26"
        },
        "And you must not bring any detestable thing into your house, or you, like it, will be set apart for destruction. You are to utterly detest and abhor it, because it is set apart for destruction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "8",
      "sid": "DEU 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Remember the LORD Your God"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 8:1"
        },
        "You must carefully follow every commandment I am giving you today, so that you may live and multiply, and enter and possess the land that the LORD swore ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to give"
          ]
        },
        " your fathers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 8:2"
        },
        "Remember that these forty years the LORD your God led you all the way in the wilderness, so that He might humble you and test you in order to know what was in your heart, whether or not you would keep His commandments."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 8:3"
        },
        "He humbled you, and in your hunger He gave you manna to eat, which neither ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        " nor your fathers had known, so that you might understand that man does not live on bread alone, but on every word that comes from the mouth of the LORD.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 4:4",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 4:4"
                  ]
                },
                " and Luke 4:4"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 8:4"
        },
        "Your clothing did not wear out and your feet did not swell during these forty years."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 8:5"
        },
        "So know in your heart that just as a man disciplines his son, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so"
          ]
        },
        " the LORD your God disciplines you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 8:6"
        },
        "Therefore you shall keep the commandments of the LORD your God, walking in His ways and fearing Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 8:7"
        },
        "For the LORD your God is bringing you into a good land, a land of brooks and fountains and springs that flow through the valleys and hills; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 8:8"
        },
        "a land of wheat, barley, vines, fig trees, and pomegranates; a land of olive oil and honey; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 8:9"
        },
        "a land where you will eat food without scarcity, where you will lack nothing; a land whose rocks are iron and whose hills are ready to be mined for copper. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 8:10"
        },
        "When you eat and are satisfied, you are to bless the LORD your God for the good land that He has given you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 8:11"
        },
        "Be careful not to forget the LORD your God by failing to keep His commandments and ordinances and statutes, which I am giving you this day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 8:12"
        },
        "Otherwise, when you eat and are satisfied, when you build fine houses in which to dwell, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 8:13"
        },
        "and when your herds and flocks grow large and your silver and gold increase and all that you have is multiplied, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 8:14"
        },
        "then your heart will become proud, and you will forget the LORD your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 8:15"
        },
        "He led you through the vast and terrifying wilderness with its venomous snakes and scorpions, a thirsty and waterless ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "land"
          ]
        },
        ". He brought you water from the rock of flint. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 8:16"
        },
        "He fed you in the wilderness with manna that your fathers had not known, in order to humble you and test you, so that in the end He might cause you to prosper."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 8:17"
        },
        "You might say in your heart, “The power and strength of my hands have made this wealth for me.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 8:18"
        },
        "But remember that it is the LORD your God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " gives you the power to gain wealth, in order to confirm His covenant that He swore to your fathers even to this day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 8:19"
        },
        "If you ever forget the LORD your God and go after other gods to worship and bow down to them, I testify against you today that you will surely perish. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 8:20"
        },
        "Like the nations that the LORD has destroyed before you, so you will perish if you do not obey the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "9",
      "sid": "DEU 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Assurance of Victory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 9:1"
        },
        "Hear, O Israel: Today you are about to cross the Jordan to go in and dispossess nations greater and stronger than you, with large cities fortified to the heavens. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 9:2"
        },
        "The people are strong and tall, the descendants of the Anakim. You know about them, and you have heard it said, “Who can stand up to the sons of Anak?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 9:3"
        },
        "But understand that today the LORD your God goes across ahead of you as a consuming fire; He will destroy them and subdue them before you. And you will drive them out and annihilate them swiftly, as the LORD has promised you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 9:4"
        },
        "When the LORD your God has driven them out before you, do not say in your heart, “Because of my righteousness the LORD has brought me in to possess this land.” Rather, the LORD is driving out these nations before you because of their wickedness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 9:5"
        },
        "It is not because of your righteousness or uprightness of heart that you are going in to possess their land, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " because of their wickedness that the LORD your God is driving out these nations before you, to keep the promise He swore to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 9:6"
        },
        "Understand, then, that it is not because of your righteousness that the LORD your God is giving you this good land to possess, for you are a stiff-necked people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Golden Calf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 32:1-35",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 32:1–35"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 7:39-43",
          "content": [
            "Acts 7:39–43"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 9:7"
        },
        "Remember this, and never forget how you provoked the LORD your God in the wilderness. From the day you left the land of Egypt until you reached this place, you have been rebelling against the LORD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 9:8"
        },
        "At Horeb",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " you provoked the LORD, and He was angry enough to destroy you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 9:9"
        },
        "When I went up on the mountain to receive the tablets of stone, the tablets of the covenant that the LORD made with you, I stayed on the mountain forty days and forty nights. I ate no bread and drank no water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 9:10"
        },
        "Then the LORD gave me the two stone tablets, inscribed by the finger of God with the exact words that the LORD spoke to you out of the fire on the mountain on the day of the assembly. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 9:11"
        },
        "And at the end of forty days and forty nights, the LORD gave me the two stone tablets, the tablets of the covenant. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 9:12"
        },
        "And the LORD said to me, “Get up and go down from here at once, for your people, whom you brought out of Egypt, have corrupted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "themselves"
          ]
        },
        ". How quickly they have turned aside from the way that I commanded them! They have made for themselves a molten image.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 9:13"
        },
        "The LORD also said to me, “I have seen this people, and they are indeed a stiff-necked people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 9:14"
        },
        "Leave Me alone, so that I may destroy them and blot out their name from under heaven. Then I will make you into a nation mightier and greater than they ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 9:15"
        },
        "So I went back down the mountain while it was blazing with fire, with the two tablets of the covenant in my hands. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 9:16"
        },
        "And I saw how you had sinned against the LORD your God; you had made for yourselves a molten calf. You had turned aside quickly from the way that the LORD had commanded you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 9:17"
        },
        "So I took the two tablets and threw them out of my hands, shattering them before your eyes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 9:18"
        },
        "Then I fell down before the LORD for forty days and forty nights, as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I had done"
          ]
        },
        " the first time. I did not eat bread or drink water because of all the sin you had committed in doing what was evil in the sight of the LORD and provoking Him to anger. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 9:19"
        },
        "For I was afraid",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "And I am greatly terrified"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 12:21",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 12:21"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of the anger and wrath that the LORD had directed against you, enough to destroy you. But the LORD listened to me this time as well."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 9:20"
        },
        "The LORD was angry enough with Aaron to destroy him, but at that time I also prayed for Aaron. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 9:21"
        },
        "And I took that sinful thing, the calf you had made, and burned it in the fire. Then I crushed it ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ground it to powder as fine as dust, and I cast it into the stream that came down from the mountain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 9:22"
        },
        "You continued to provoke the LORD at Taberah,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Taberah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "burning"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "NUM 11:3",
                  "content": [
                    "Numbers 11:3"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " at Massah,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Massah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "testing"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 17:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 17:7"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and at Kibroth-hattaavah.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Kibroth-hattaavah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "graves of craving"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "NUM 11:34",
                  "content": [
                    "Numbers 11:34"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 9:23"
        },
        "And when the LORD sent you out from Kadesh-barnea, He said, “Go up and possess the land that I have given you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "But you rebelled against the command of the LORD your God. You neither believed Him nor obeyed Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 9:24"
        },
        "You have been rebelling against the LORD since the day I came to know you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 9:25"
        },
        "So I fell down before the LORD for forty days and forty nights, because the LORD had said He would destroy you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 9:26"
        },
        "And I prayed to the LORD and said, “O Lord GOD, do not destroy Your people, Your inheritance, whom You redeemed through Your greatness and brought out of Egypt with a mighty hand. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 9:27"
        },
        "Remember Your servants Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. Overlook the stubbornness of this people and the wickedness of their sin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 9:28"
        },
        "Otherwise, those in the land from which You brought us out will say, ‘Because the LORD was not able to bring them into the land He had promised them, and because He hated them, He has brought them out to kill them in the wilderness.’ ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 9:29"
        },
        "But they are Your people, Your inheritance, whom You brought out by Your great power and outstretched arm.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "10",
      "sid": "DEU 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "New Stone Tablets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 34:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 34:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 10:1"
        },
        "At that time the LORD said to me, “Chisel out two stone tablets like the originals, come up to Me on the mountain, and make an ark of wood. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 10:2"
        },
        "And I will write on the tablets the words that were on the first tablets, which you broke; and you are to place them in the ark.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 10:3"
        },
        "So I made an ark of acacia wood, chiseled out two stone tablets like the originals, and went up the mountain with the two tablets in my hands. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 10:4"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the LORD"
          ]
        },
        " wrote on the tablets what had been written previously, the Ten Commandments",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Ten Words"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " that He had spoken to you on the mountain out of the fire on the day of the assembly. The LORD gave them to me, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 10:5"
        },
        "and I went back down the mountain and placed the tablets in the ark I had made, as the LORD had commanded me; and there they have remained."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 10:6"
        },
        "The Israelites traveled from Beeroth Bene-jaakan",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "from the wells of the Bene-jaakan"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to Moserah, where Aaron died and was buried, and Eleazar his son succeeded him as priest. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 10:7"
        },
        "From there they traveled to Gudgodah, and from Gudgodah to Jotbathah, a land with streams of water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 10:8"
        },
        "At that time the LORD set apart the tribe of Levi to carry the ark of the covenant of the LORD, to stand before the LORD to serve Him, and to pronounce blessings in His name, as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they do"
          ]
        },
        " to this day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 10:9"
        },
        "That is why Levi has no portion or inheritance among his brothers; the LORD is his inheritance, as the LORD your God promised him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 10:10"
        },
        "I stayed on the mountain forty days and forty nights, like the first time, and that time the LORD again listened to me ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " agreed not to destroy you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 10:11"
        },
        "Then the LORD said to me, “Get up. Continue your journey ahead of the people, that they may enter and possess the land that I swore to their fathers to give them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Call to Obedience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOS 24:14-28",
          "content": [
            "Joshua 24:14–28"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 10:12"
        },
        "And now, O Israel, what does the LORD your God ask of you but to fear the LORD your God by walking in all His ways, to love Him, to serve the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 10:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " to keep the commandments and statutes of the LORD that I am giving you this day for your own good?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 10:14"
        },
        "Behold, to the LORD your God belong the heavens, even the highest heavens, and the earth and everything in it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 10:15"
        },
        "Yet the LORD has set His affection on your fathers and loved them. And He has chosen you, their descendants after them, above all the peoples, even to this day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 10:16"
        },
        "Circumcise your hearts, therefore, and stiffen your necks no more. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 10:17"
        },
        "For the LORD your God is God of gods and Lord of lords, the great, mighty, and awesome God, showing no partiality and accepting no bribe. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 10:18"
        },
        "He executes justice for the fatherless and widow, and He loves the foreigner, giving him food and clothing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 10:19"
        },
        "So you also must love the foreigner, since you yourselves were foreigners in the land of Egypt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 10:20"
        },
        "You are to fear the LORD your God and serve Him. Hold fast to Him and take your oaths in His name. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 10:21"
        },
        "He is your praise and He is your God, who has done for you these great and awesome wonders that your eyes have seen. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 10:22"
        },
        "Your fathers went down to Egypt, seventy in all, and now the LORD your God has made you as numerous as the stars in the sky."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "11",
      "sid": "DEU 11"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Obedience and Discipline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 4:1-14",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 4:1–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 11:1"
        },
        "You shall therefore love the LORD your God and always keep His charge, His statutes, His ordinances, and His commandments."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 11:2"
        },
        "Know this day that it is not your children who have known and seen the discipline of the LORD your God: His greatness, His mighty hand, and His outstretched arm; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 11:3"
        },
        "the signs and works He did in Egypt to Pharaoh king of Egypt and all his land; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 11:4"
        },
        "what He did to the Egyptian army and horses and chariots when He made the waters of the Red Sea",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Sea of Reeds"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " engulf them as they pursued you, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "how"
          ]
        },
        " He destroyed them completely, even to this day; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 11:5"
        },
        "what He did for you in the wilderness until you reached this place; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 11:6"
        },
        "and what He did in the midst of all the Israelites to Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab the Reubenite, when the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them, their households, their tents, and every living thing that belonged to them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 11:7"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " your own eyes ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " have seen every great work that the LORD has done."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "God’s Great Blessings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOS 1:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Joshua 1:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 11:8"
        },
        "You shall therefore keep every commandment I am giving you today, so that you may have the strength to go in and possess the land that you are crossing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Jordan"
          ]
        },
        " to possess, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 11:9"
        },
        "and so that you may live long in the land that the LORD swore to your fathers to give them and their descendants, a land flowing with milk and honey."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 11:10"
        },
        "For the land that you are entering to possess is not like the land of Egypt, from which you have come, where you sowed your seed and irrigated on foot, like a vegetable garden. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 11:11"
        },
        "But the land that you are crossing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Jordan"
          ]
        },
        " to possess is a land of mountains and valleys that drinks in the rain from heaven. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 11:12"
        },
        "It is a land for which the LORD your God cares; the eyes of the LORD your God are always on it, from the beginning to the end of the year."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 11:13"
        },
        "So if you carefully obey the commandments I am giving you today, to love the LORD your God and to serve Him with all your heart and with all your soul, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 11:14"
        },
        "then I will provide",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew; SP, LXX, and Vulgate "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "He will provide"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 15"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " rain for your land in season, the autumn and spring rains, that you may gather your grain, new wine, and oil. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 11:15"
        },
        "And I will provide grass in the fields for your livestock, and you will eat and be satisfied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 11:16"
        },
        "But be careful that you are not enticed to turn aside to worship and bow down to other gods, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 11:17"
        },
        "or the anger of the LORD will be kindled against you. He will shut the heavens so that there will be no rain, nor will the land yield its produce, and you will soon perish from the good land that the LORD is giving you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Remember God’s Words"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 11:18"
        },
        "Fix these words of mine in your hearts and minds; tie them as reminders on your hands and bind them on your foreheads. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 11:19"
        },
        "Teach them to your children, speaking about them when you sit at home and when you walk along the road, when you lie down and when you get up. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 11:20"
        },
        "Write them on the doorposts of your houses and on your gates, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 11:21"
        },
        "so that as long as the heavens are above the earth, your days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and those"
          ]
        },
        " of your children may be multiplied in the land that the LORD swore to give your fathers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 11:22"
        },
        "For if you carefully keep all these commandments I am giving you to follow— to love the LORD your God, to walk in all His ways, and to hold fast to Him— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 11:23"
        },
        "then the LORD will drive out all these nations before you, and you will dispossess nations greater and stronger than you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 11:24"
        },
        "Every place where the sole of your foot treads will be yours. Your territory will extend from the wilderness to Lebanon, and from the Euphrates River to the Western Sea.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 11:25"
        },
        "No man will be able to stand against you; the LORD your God will put the fear and dread of you upon all the land, wherever you set foot, as He has promised you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Blessing and a Curse"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 11:26"
        },
        "See, today I am setting before you a blessing and a curse — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 11:27"
        },
        "a blessing if you obey the commandments of the LORD your God that I am giving you today, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 11:28"
        },
        "but a curse if you disobey the commandments of the LORD your God and turn aside from the path I command you today by following other gods, which you have not known."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 11:29"
        },
        "When the LORD your God brings you into the land you are entering to possess, you are to proclaim the blessing on Mount Gerizim and the curse on Mount Ebal. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 11:30"
        },
        "Are not these mountains across the Jordan, west of the road toward the sunset, in the land of the Canaanites who live in the Arabah opposite Gilgal near the Oak",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "SP, LXX, and Syriac (see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 12:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 12:6"
                  ]
                },
                "); Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Oaks "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Terebinths "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Great Trees"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of Moreh?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 11:31"
        },
        "For you are about to cross the Jordan to enter and possess the land that the LORD your God is giving you. When you take possession of it and settle in it, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 11:32"
        },
        "be careful to follow all the statutes and ordinances that I am setting before you today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "12",
      "sid": "DEU 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "One Place for Worship"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 12:1"
        },
        "These ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " the statutes and ordinances you must be careful to follow all the days you live in the land that the LORD, the God of your fathers, has given you to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 12:2"
        },
        "Destroy completely all the places where the nations you are dispossessing have served their gods— atop the high mountains, on the hills, and under every green tree. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 12:3"
        },
        "Tear down their altars, smash their sacred pillars, burn up their Asherah poles, cut down the idols of their gods, and wipe out their names from every place. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 12:4"
        },
        "You shall not worship the LORD your God in this way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 12:5"
        },
        "Instead, you must seek the place the LORD your God will choose from among all your tribes to establish as a dwelling for His Name, and there you must go. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 12:6"
        },
        "To that place you are to bring your burnt offerings and sacrifices, your tithes and heave offerings, your vow offerings and freewill offerings, as well as the firstborn of your herds and flocks. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 12:7"
        },
        "There, in the presence of the LORD your God, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you and"
          ]
        },
        " your households shall eat and rejoice in all you do, because the LORD your God has blessed you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 12:8"
        },
        "You are not to do as we are doing here today, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " everyone ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " what seems right in his own eyes. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 12:9"
        },
        "For you have not yet come to the resting place and the inheritance that the LORD your God is giving you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 12:10"
        },
        "When you cross the Jordan and live in the land that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance, and He gives you rest from all the enemies around you and you dwell securely, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 12:11"
        },
        "then the LORD your God will choose a dwelling for His Name. And there you are to bring everything I command you: your burnt offerings and sacrifices, your tithes and special gifts, and all the choice offerings you vow to the LORD. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 12:12"
        },
        "And you shall rejoice before the LORD your God— you, your sons and daughters, your menservants and maidservants, and the Levite within your gates, since he has no portion or inheritance among you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 12:13"
        },
        "Be careful not to offer your burnt offerings in just any place you see; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 12:14"
        },
        "you must offer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " only in the place the LORD will choose in one of your tribal territories, and there you shall do all that I command you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 12:15"
        },
        "But whenever you want, you may slaughter and eat meat within any of your gates, according to the blessing the LORD your God has given you. Both the ceremonially clean and unclean may eat it as they would a gazelle or deer, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 12:16"
        },
        "but you must not eat the blood; pour it on the ground like water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 12:17"
        },
        "Within your gates you must not eat the tithe of your grain or new wine or oil, the firstborn of your herds or flocks, any of the offerings that you have vowed to give, or your freewill offerings or special gifts. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 12:18"
        },
        "Instead, you must eat them in the presence of the LORD your God at the place the LORD your God will choose— you, your sons and daughters, your menservants and maidservants, and the Levite within your gates. Rejoice before the LORD your God in all you do, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 12:19"
        },
        "and be careful not to neglect the Levites as long as you live in your land."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 12:20"
        },
        "When the LORD your God expands your territory as He has promised, and you crave meat and say, “I want to eat meat,” you may eat it whenever you want. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 12:21"
        },
        "If the place where the LORD your God chooses to put His Name is too far from you, then you may slaughter any of the herd or flock He has given you, as I have commanded you, and you may eat it within your gates whenever you want. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 12:22"
        },
        "Indeed, you may eat it as you would eat a gazelle or deer; both the ceremonially unclean and the clean may eat it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 12:23"
        },
        "Only be sure not to eat the blood, because the blood is the life, and you must not eat the life with the meat. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 12:24"
        },
        "You must not eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the blood"
          ]
        },
        "; pour it on the ground like water. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 12:25"
        },
        "Do not eat it, so that it may go well with you and your children after you, because you will be doing what is right in the eyes of the LORD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 12:26"
        },
        "But you are to take your holy things and your vow offerings and go to the place the LORD will choose. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 12:27"
        },
        "Present the meat and blood of your burnt offerings on the altar of the LORD your God. The blood of your other sacrifices must be poured out beside the altar of the LORD your God, but you may eat the meat. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 12:28"
        },
        "Be careful to obey all these things I command you, so that it may always go well with you and your children after you, because you will be doing what is good and right in the eyes of the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Warning against Idolatry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 4:15-31",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 4:15–31"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EZK 6:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Ezekiel 6:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 12:29"
        },
        "When the LORD your God cuts off before you the nations you are entering to dispossess, and you drive them out and live in their land, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 12:30"
        },
        "be careful not to be ensnared by their ways after they have been destroyed before you. Do not inquire about their gods, asking, “How do these nations serve their gods? I will do likewise.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 12:31"
        },
        "You must not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "worship"
          ]
        },
        " the LORD your God in this way, because they practice for their gods every abomination which the LORD hates. They even burn their sons and daughters in the fire ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as sacrifices"
          ]
        },
        " to their gods."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 12:32"
        },
        "See that you do everything I command you; do not add to it or subtract from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "13",
      "sid": "DEU 13"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Idolaters to Be Put to Death"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 13:1"
        },
        "If a prophet or dreamer of dreams arises among you and proclaims a sign or wonder to you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 13:2"
        },
        "and if the sign or wonder he has spoken to you comes about, but he says, “Let us follow other gods (which you have not known) and let us worship them,” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 13:3"
        },
        "you must not listen to the words of that prophet or dreamer. For the LORD your God is testing you to find out whether you love ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " with all your heart and with all your soul. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 13:4"
        },
        "You are to follow the LORD your God and fear Him. Keep His commandments and listen to His voice; serve Him and hold fast to Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 13:5"
        },
        "Such a prophet or dreamer must be put to death, because he has advocated rebellion against the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt and redeemed you from the house of slavery; he has tried to turn you from the way in which the LORD your God has commanded you to walk. So you must purge the evil from among you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 5:13",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 5:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 13:6"
        },
        "If your very own brother, or your son or daughter, or the wife you embrace,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the wife of your bosom"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " or your closest friend secretly entices you, saying, “Let us go and worship other gods” (which neither you nor your fathers have known, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 13:7"
        },
        "the gods of the peoples around you, whether near or far, whether from one end of the earth or the other), ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 13:8"
        },
        "you must not yield to him or listen to him. Show him no pity, and do not spare him or shield him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 13:9"
        },
        "Instead, you must surely kill him. Your hand must be the first against him to put him to death, and then the hands of all the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 13:10"
        },
        "Stone him to death for trying to turn you away from the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 13:11"
        },
        "Then all Israel will hear and be afraid, and will never again do such a wicked thing among you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Idolatrous Cities to Be Destroyed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 13:12"
        },
        "If, regarding one of the cities the LORD your God is giving you to inhabit, you hear it said ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 13:13"
        },
        "that wicked men have arisen from among you and have led the people of their city astray, saying, “Let us go and serve other gods” (which you have not known), ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 13:14"
        },
        "then you must inquire, investigate, and interrogate thoroughly. And if it is established with certainty that this abomination has been committed among you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 13:15"
        },
        "you must surely put the inhabitants of that city to the sword. Devote to destruction",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "cherem "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; similarly in verse 17."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its people"
          ]
        },
        " and livestock."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 13:16"
        },
        "And you are to gather all its plunder in the middle of the public square, and completely burn the city and all its plunder as a whole burnt offering to the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The city"
          ]
        },
        " must remain a mound of ruins forever, never to be rebuilt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 13:17"
        },
        "Nothing devoted to destruction shall cling to your hands, so that the LORD will turn from His fierce anger, grant you mercy, show you compassion, and multiply you as He swore to your fathers, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 13:18"
        },
        "because you obey the LORD your God, keeping all His commandments I am giving you today ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " doing what is right in the eyes of the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "14",
      "sid": "DEU 14"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Clean and Unclean Animals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 11:1-47",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 11:1–47"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 10:9-16",
          "content": [
            "Acts 10:9–16"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 14:1"
        },
        "You are sons of the LORD your God; do not cut yourselves or shave your foreheads on behalf of the dead, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 14:2"
        },
        "for you are a people holy to the LORD your God. The LORD has chosen you to be a people for His prized possession out of all the peoples on the face of the earth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 14:3"
        },
        "You must not eat any detestable thing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 14:4"
        },
        "These are the animals that you may eat:",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "14:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "The precise identification of some of the birds and animals in this chapter is uncertain."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "The ox, the sheep, the goat,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 14:5"
        },
        "the deer, the gazelle, the roe deer,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "the wild goat, the ibex, the antelope,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "and the mountain sheep."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 14:6"
        },
        "You may eat any animal that has a split hoof divided in two and that chews the cud."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 14:7"
        },
        "But of those that chew the cud or have a completely divided hoof, you are not to eat the following:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "the camel,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "the rabbit,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " the rock badger.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "14:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the coney "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the hyrax"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "Although they chew the cud, they do not have a divided hoof. They are unclean for you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 14:8"
        },
        "as well as the pig; though it has a divided hoof, it does not chew the cud. It is unclean for you. You must not eat its meat or touch its carcass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 14:9"
        },
        "Of all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the creatures"
          ]
        },
        " that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "live"
          ]
        },
        " in the water, you may eat anything with fins and scales, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 14:10"
        },
        "but you may not eat anything that does not have fins and scales; it is unclean for you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 14:11"
        },
        "You may eat any clean bird, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 14:12"
        },
        "but these you may not eat:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "the eagle, the bearded vulture, the black vulture,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 14:13"
        },
        "the red kite, the falcon, any kind of kite,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 14:14"
        },
        "any kind of raven,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 14:15"
        },
        "the ostrich,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "14:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the daughter of the ostrich "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the daughter of the owl"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " the screech owl, the gull, any kind of hawk,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 14:16"
        },
        "the little owl, the great owl, the white owl,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 14:17"
        },
        "the desert owl, the osprey, the cormorant,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 14:18"
        },
        "the stork, any kind of heron,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        "the hoopoe, or the bat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 14:19"
        },
        "All flying insects are unclean for you; they may not be eaten. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 14:20"
        },
        "But you may eat any clean bird."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 14:21"
        },
        "You are not to eat any carcass; you may give it to the foreigner residing within your gates, and he may eat it, or you may sell it to a foreigner. For you are a holy people belonging to the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "You must not cook a young goat in its mother’s milk."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Giving Tithes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 27:30-34",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 27:30–34"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 26:1-15",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 26:1–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NEH 13:10-14",
          "content": [
            "Nehemiah 13:10–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 14:22"
        },
        "You must be sure to set aside a tenth of all the produce brought forth each year from your fields. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 14:23"
        },
        "And you are to eat a tenth of your grain, new wine, and oil, and the firstborn of your herds and flocks, in the presence of the LORD your God at the place He will choose as a dwelling for His Name, so that you may learn to fear the LORD your God always."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 14:24"
        },
        "But if the distance is too great for you to carry that with which the LORD your God has blessed you, because the place where the LORD your God will choose to put His Name is too far away, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 14:25"
        },
        "then exchange it for money, take the money in your hand, and go to the place the LORD your God will choose. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 14:26"
        },
        "Then you may spend the money on anything you desire: cattle, sheep, wine, strong drink, or anything you wish. You are to feast there in the presence of the LORD your God and rejoice with your household. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 14:27"
        },
        "And do not neglect the Levite within your gates, since he has no portion or inheritance among you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 14:28"
        },
        "At the end of every three years, bring a tenth of all your produce for that year and lay ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " up within your gates. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 14:29"
        },
        "Then the Levite (because he has no portion or inheritance among you), the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow within your gates may come and eat and be satisfied. And the LORD your God will bless you in all the work of your hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "15",
      "sid": "DEU 15"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Seventh Year"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 23:10-13",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 23:10–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 25:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 25:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 15:1"
        },
        "At the end of every seven years you must cancel debts. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 15:2"
        },
        "This is the manner of remission: Every creditor shall cancel what he has loaned to his neighbor. He is not to collect anything from his neighbor or brother, because the LORD’s time of release has been proclaimed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 15:3"
        },
        "You may collect something from a foreigner, but you must forgive whatever your brother owes you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 15:4"
        },
        "There will be no poor among you, however, because the LORD will surely bless you in the land that the LORD your God is giving you to possess as an inheritance, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 15:5"
        },
        "if only you obey the LORD your God and are careful to follow all these commandments I am giving you today. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 15:6"
        },
        "When the LORD your God blesses you as He has promised, you will lend to many nations but borrow from none; you will rule over many nations but be ruled by none."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Generosity in Lending and Giving"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 6:1-4",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 6:1–4"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 15:7"
        },
        "If there is a poor man among your brothers within any of the gates in the land that the LORD your God is giving you, then you are not to harden",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "15:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "make strong "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "make courageous"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " your heart ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " shut your hand from your poor brother. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 15:8"
        },
        "Instead, you are to open your hand to him and freely loan him whatever he needs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 15:9"
        },
        "Be careful not to harbor this wicked thought in your heart: “The seventh year, the year of release, is near,” so that you look upon your poor brother begrudgingly and give him nothing. He will cry out to the LORD against you, and you will be guilty of sin."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 15:10"
        },
        "Give generously to him, and do not let your heart be grieved ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when you do so"
          ]
        },
        ". And because of this the LORD your God will bless you in all your work and in everything to which you put your hand. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 15:11"
        },
        "For there will never cease to be poor in the land; that is why I am commanding you to open wide your hand to your brother and to the poor and needy in your land."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Hebrew Servants"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 21:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 21:1–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 15:12"
        },
        "If a fellow Hebrew, a man or a woman, is sold",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "15:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "sells himself"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to you and serves you six years, then in the seventh year you must set him free."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 15:13"
        },
        "And when you release him, do not send him away empty-handed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 15:14"
        },
        "You are to furnish him liberally from your flock, your threshing floor, and your winepress. You shall give to him as the LORD your God has blessed you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 15:15"
        },
        "Remember that you were slaves in the land of Egypt, and the LORD your God redeemed you; that is why I am giving you this command today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 15:16"
        },
        "But if your servant says to you, ‘I do not want to leave you,’ because he loves you and your household and is well off with you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 15:17"
        },
        "then take an awl and pierce ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " through his ear into the door, and he will become your servant for life. And treat your maidservant the same way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 15:18"
        },
        "Do not regard it as a hardship to set ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your servant"
          ]
        },
        " free, because his six years of service were worth twice the wages of a hired hand. And the LORD your God will bless you in all you do."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Firstborn Animals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 13:1-16",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 13:1–16"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 15:19"
        },
        "You must set apart to the LORD your God every firstborn male produced by your herds and flocks. You are not to put the firstborn of your oxen to work, nor are you to shear the firstborn of your flock. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 15:20"
        },
        "Each year you and your household are to eat it before the LORD your God in the place the LORD will choose."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 15:21"
        },
        "But if ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "an animal"
          ]
        },
        " has a defect, is lame or blind, or has any serious flaw, you must not sacrifice it to the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 15:22"
        },
        "Eat it within your gates; both the ceremonially unclean and clean ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "may eat it"
          ]
        },
        " as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they would"
          ]
        },
        " a gazelle or a deer. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 15:23"
        },
        "But you must not eat the blood; pour it on the ground like water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "16",
      "sid": "DEU 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 12:14-28",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 12:14–28"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 23:4-8",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 23:4–8"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 28:16-25",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 28:16–25"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 16:1"
        },
        "Observe the month of Abib",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Abib "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April; twice in this verse."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and celebrate the Passover to the LORD your God, because in the month of Abib the LORD your God brought you out of Egypt by night."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 16:2"
        },
        "You are to offer to the LORD your God the Passover sacrifice from the herd or flock in the place the LORD will choose as a dwelling for His Name. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 16:3"
        },
        "You must not eat leavened bread with it; for seven days you are to eat with it unleavened bread, the bread of affliction, because you left the land of Egypt in haste— so that you may remember for the rest of your life the day you left the land of Egypt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 16:4"
        },
        "No leaven is to be found in all your land for seven days, and none of the meat you sacrifice in the evening of the first day shall remain until morning."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 16:5"
        },
        "You are not to sacrifice the Passover animal in any of the towns that the LORD your God is giving you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 16:6"
        },
        "You must only offer the Passover sacrifice at the place the LORD your God will choose as a dwelling for His Name. Do this in the evening as the sun sets, at the same time you departed from Egypt. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 16:7"
        },
        "And you shall roast it and eat it in the place the LORD your God will choose, and in the morning you shall return to your tents."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 16:8"
        },
        "For six days you must eat unleavened bread, and on the seventh day you shall hold a solemn assembly to the LORD your God, and you must not do any work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Feast of Weeks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 28:26-31",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 28:26–31"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 16:9"
        },
        "You are to count off seven weeks ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the time"
          ]
        },
        " you first put the sickle to the standing grain. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 16:10"
        },
        "And you shall celebrate the Feast of Weeks",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Shavuot; see footnotes for verse 16."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to the LORD your God with a freewill offering that you give in proportion to how the LORD your God has blessed you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 16:11"
        },
        "and you shall rejoice before the LORD your God in the place He will choose as a dwelling for His Name — you, your sons and daughters, your menservants and maidservants, and the Levite within your gates, as well as the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widows among you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 16:12"
        },
        "Remember that you were slaves in Egypt, and carefully follow these statutes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Feast of Tabernacles"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 29:12-40",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 29:12–40"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 16:13"
        },
        "You are to celebrate the Feast of Tabernacles",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Booths "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Shelters"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see footnotes for verse 16."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " for seven days after you have gathered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the produce of"
          ]
        },
        " your threshing floor and your winepress. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 16:14"
        },
        "And you shall rejoice in your feast— you, your sons and daughters, your menservants and maidservants, and the Levite, as well as the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widows among you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 16:15"
        },
        "For seven days you shall celebrate a feast to the LORD your God in the place He will choose, because the LORD your God will bless you in all your produce and in all the work of your hands, so that your joy will be complete."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 16:16"
        },
        "Three times a year all your men are to appear before the LORD your God in the place He will choose: at the Feast of Unleavened Bread,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 12:14-20",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 12:14–20"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " the Feast of Weeks,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Harvest"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 23:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 23:16"
                  ]
                },
                ") or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Pentecost"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ACT 2:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Acts 2:1"
                  ]
                },
                ")."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and the Feast of Tabernacles.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Booths "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Shelters "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "and originally called "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Ingathering"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 23:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 23:16"
                  ]
                },
                " and Exodus 34:22)."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " No one should appear before the LORD empty-handed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 16:17"
        },
        "Everyone must appear with a gift as he is able, according to the blessing the LORD your God has given you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Judges and Justice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 16:18"
        },
        "You are to appoint judges and officials for your tribes in every town that the LORD your God is giving you. They are to judge the people with righteous judgment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 16:19"
        },
        "Do not deny justice or show partiality. Do not accept a bribe, for a bribe blinds the eyes of the wise and twists the words of the righteous."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 16:20"
        },
        "Pursue justice, and justice alone, so that you may live, and you may possess the land that the LORD your God is giving you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Forbidden Forms of Worship"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 16:21"
        },
        "Do not set up any wooden Asherah pole next to the altar you will build for the LORD your God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 16:22"
        },
        "and do not set up for yourselves a sacred pillar, which the LORD your God hates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "17",
      "sid": "DEU 17"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Detestable Sacrifices"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 17:1"
        },
        "You shall not sacrifice to the LORD your God an ox or a sheep with any defect ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " serious flaw, for that is detestable to the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Purge the Idolater"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 17:2"
        },
        "If a man or woman among you in one of the towns that the LORD your God gives you is found doing evil in the sight of the LORD your God by transgressing His covenant ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 17:3"
        },
        "and going to worship other gods, bowing down to them or to the sun or moon or any of the host of heaven— which I have forbidden— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 17:4"
        },
        "and if it is reported and you hear about it, you must investigate it thoroughly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "If the report is true and such an abomination has happened in Israel, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 17:5"
        },
        "you must bring out to your gates the man or woman who has done this evil thing, and you must stone that person to death. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 17:6"
        },
        "On the testimony of two or three witnesses a man shall be put to death, but he shall not be executed on the testimony of a lone witness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 17:7"
        },
        "The hands of the witnesses shall be the first in putting him to death, and after that, the hands of all the people. So you must purge the evil from among you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 5:13",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 5:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Courts of Law"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 17:8"
        },
        "If a case is too difficult for you to judge, whether the controversy within your gates is regarding bloodshed, lawsuits, or assaults, you must go up to the place the LORD your God will choose. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 17:9"
        },
        "You are to go to the Levitical priests and to the judge who presides at that time. Inquire of them, and they will give you a verdict in the case."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 17:10"
        },
        "You must abide by the verdict they give you at the place the LORD will choose. Be careful to do everything they instruct you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 17:11"
        },
        "according to the terms of law they give and the verdict they proclaim. Do not turn aside to the right or to the left from the decision they declare to you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 17:12"
        },
        "But the man who acts presumptuously, refusing to listen either to the priest who stands there to serve the LORD your God, or to the judge, must be put to death. You must purge the evil from Israel. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 17:13"
        },
        "Then all the people will hear and be afraid, and will no longer behave arrogantly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Guidelines for a King"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1SA 8:1-9",
          "content": [
            "1 Samuel 8:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 17:14"
        },
        "When you enter the land that the LORD your God is giving you and have taken possession of it and settled in it, and you say, “Let us set a king over us like all the nations around us,” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 17:15"
        },
        "you are to appoint over yourselves the king whom the LORD your God shall choose. Appoint a king from among your brothers; you are not to set over yourselves a foreigner who is not one of your brothers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 17:16"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the king"
          ]
        },
        " must not acquire many horses for himself ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " send the people back to Egypt to acquire more horses, for the LORD has said, ‘You are never to go back that way again.’ ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 17:17"
        },
        "He must not take many wives for himself, lest his heart go astray. He must not accumulate for himself large amounts of silver and gold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 17:18"
        },
        "When he is seated on his royal throne, he must write for himself a copy of this instruction on a scroll in the presence of the Levitical priests. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 17:19"
        },
        "It is to remain with him, and he is to read from it all the days of his life, so that he may learn to fear the LORD his God by carefully observing all the words of this instruction and these statutes. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 17:20"
        },
        "Then his heart will not be exalted above his countrymen, and he will not turn aside from the commandment, to the right or to the left, in order that he and his sons may reign many years over his kingdom in Israel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "18",
      "sid": "DEU 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Provision for Priests and Levites"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1CO 9:1-18",
          "content": [
            "1 Corinthians 9:1–18"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 18:1"
        },
        "The Levitical priests — indeed the whole tribe of Levi — shall have no portion or inheritance with Israel. They are to eat the food offerings to the LORD; that is their inheritance. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 18:2"
        },
        "Although they have no inheritance among their brothers, the LORD ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " their inheritance, as He promised them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 18:3"
        },
        "This shall be the priests’ share from the people who offer a sacrifice, whether a bull or a sheep: the priests are to be given the shoulder, the jowls, and the stomach. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 18:4"
        },
        "You are to give them the firstfruits of your grain, new wine, and oil, and the first wool sheared from your flock. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 18:5"
        },
        "For the LORD your God has chosen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Levi"
          ]
        },
        " and his sons out of all your tribes to stand and minister in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " name for all time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 18:6"
        },
        "Now if a Levite moves from any town of residence throughout Israel and comes in all earnestness to the place the LORD will choose, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 18:7"
        },
        "then he shall serve in the name of the LORD his God like all his fellow Levites who stand there before the LORD. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 18:8"
        },
        "They shall eat equal portions, even though he has received ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "money"
          ]
        },
        " from the sale of his father’s estate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Sorcery Forbidden"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 8:9-25",
          "content": [
            "Acts 8:9–25"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 18:9"
        },
        "When you enter the land that the LORD your God is giving you, do not imitate the detestable ways of the nations there. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 18:10"
        },
        "Let no one be found among you who sacrifices his son or daughter in the fire,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "makes his son or his daughter pass through the fire"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " practices divination ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " conjury, interprets omens, practices sorcery, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 18:11"
        },
        "casts spells, consults a medium or spiritist, or inquires of the dead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 18:12"
        },
        "For whoever does these things is detestable to the LORD. And because of these detestable things, the LORD your God is driving out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the nations"
          ]
        },
        " before you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 18:13"
        },
        "You must be blameless before the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 18:14"
        },
        "Though these nations, which you will dispossess, listen to conjurers and diviners, the LORD your God has not permitted you to do so."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Prophet Like Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 3:11-26",
          "content": [
            "Acts 3:11–26"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 18:15"
        },
        "The LORD your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers. You must listen to him.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ACT 3:22",
                  "content": [
                    "Acts 3:22"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 18:16"
        },
        "This is what you asked of the LORD your God at Horeb",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " on the day of the assembly, when you said, “Let us not hear the voice of the LORD our God or see this great fire anymore, so that we will not die!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 18:17"
        },
        "Then the LORD said to me, “They have spoken well. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 18:18"
        },
        "I will raise up for them a prophet like you from among their brothers. I will put My words in his mouth, and he will tell them everything I command him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 18:19"
        },
        "And I will hold accountable anyone who does not listen to My words that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the prophet"
          ]
        },
        " speaks in My name.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ACT 3:23",
                  "content": [
                    "Acts 3:23"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 18:20"
        },
        "But if any prophet dares to speak a message in My name that I have not commanded him to speak, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " to speak in the name of other gods, that prophet must be put to death.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 18:21"
        },
        "You may ask in your heart, “How can we recognize a message that the LORD has not spoken?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 18:22"
        },
        "When a prophet speaks in the name of the LORD and the message does not come to pass ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " come true, that is a message the LORD has not spoken. The prophet has spoken presumptuously. Do not be afraid of him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "19",
      "sid": "DEU 19"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Cities of Refuge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 35:9-34",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 35:9–34"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 4:41-43",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 4:41–43"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOS 20:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Joshua 20:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 19:1"
        },
        "When the LORD your God has cut off the nations whose land He is giving you, and when you have driven them out and settled in their cities and houses, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 19:2"
        },
        "then you are to set apart for yourselves three cities within the land that the LORD your God is giving you to possess. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 19:3"
        },
        "You are to build roads for yourselves",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "You are to survey the way"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and divide into three regions the land that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance, so that any manslayer can flee to these cities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 19:4"
        },
        "Now this is the situation regarding the manslayer who flees ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to one of these cities"
          ]
        },
        " to save his life, having killed his neighbor accidentally, without intending to harm him: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 19:5"
        },
        "If he goes into the forest with his neighbor to cut timber and swings his axe to chop down a tree, but the blade flies off the handle and strikes and kills his neighbor, he may flee to one of these cities to save his life."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 19:6"
        },
        "Otherwise, the avenger of blood might pursue the manslayer in a rage, overtake him if the distance is great, and strike him dead though he did not deserve to die, since he did not intend any harm. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 19:7"
        },
        "This is why I am commanding you to set apart for yourselves three cities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 19:8"
        },
        "And if the LORD your God enlarges your territory, as He swore to your fathers, and gives you all the land He promised them, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 19:9"
        },
        "and if you carefully keep all these commandments I am giving you today, loving the LORD your God and walking in His ways at all times, then you are to add three more cities to these three."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 19:10"
        },
        "Thus innocent blood will not be shed in the land that the LORD your God is giving you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " an inheritance, so that you will not be guilty of bloodshed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 19:11"
        },
        "If, however, a man hates his neighbor and lies in wait, attacks him and kills him, and then flees to one of these cities, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 19:12"
        },
        "the elders of his city must send for him, bring him back, and hand him over to the avenger of blood to die. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 19:13"
        },
        "You must show him no pity. You are to purge from Israel the guilt of shedding innocent blood, that it may go well with you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 19:14"
        },
        "You must not move your neighbor’s boundary marker, which was set up by your ancestors ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to mark"
          ]
        },
        " the inheritance you shall receive in the land that the LORD your God is giving you to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Testimony of Two or Three Witnesses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 18:15-20",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 18:15–20"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 19:15"
        },
        "A lone witness is not sufficient to establish any wrongdoing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " sin against a man, regardless of what offense he may have committed. A matter must be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 18:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 18:16"
                  ]
                },
                " and 2 Corinthians 13:1"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 19:16"
        },
        "If a false witness testifies against someone, accusing him of a crime, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 19:17"
        },
        "both parties to the dispute must stand in the presence of the LORD, before the priests and judges who are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in office"
          ]
        },
        " at that time. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 19:18"
        },
        "The judges shall investigate thoroughly, and if the witness is proven to be a liar who has falsely accused his brother, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 19:19"
        },
        "you must do to him as he intended to do to his brother. So you must purge the evil from among you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 5:13",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 5:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 19:20"
        },
        "Then the rest ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the people"
          ]
        },
        " will hear and be afraid, and they will never again do anything so evil among you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 19:21"
        },
        "You must show no pity: life for life, eye for eye, tooth for tooth,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 5:38",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 5:38"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " hand for hand, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " foot for foot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "20",
      "sid": "DEU 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Laws of Warfare"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 20:1"
        },
        "When you go out to war against your enemies and see horses, chariots, and an army larger than yours, do not be afraid of them; for the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, is with you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 20:2"
        },
        "When you are about to go into battle, the priest is to come forward and address the army, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 20:3"
        },
        "saying to them, “Hear, O Israel, today you are going into battle with your enemies. Do not be fainthearted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " afraid; do not be alarmed or terrified because of them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 20:4"
        },
        "For the LORD your God goes with you to fight for you against your enemies, to give you the victory.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 20:5"
        },
        "Furthermore, the officers are to address the army, saying, “Has any man built a new house and not dedicated it? Let him return home, or he may die in battle and another man dedicate it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 20:6"
        },
        "Has any man planted a vineyard and not begun to enjoy its fruit? Let him return home, or he may die in battle and another man enjoy its fruit. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 20:7"
        },
        "Has any man become pledged to a woman and not married her? Let him return home, or he may die in battle and another man marry her.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 20:8"
        },
        "Then the officers shall speak further to the army, saying, “Is any man afraid or fainthearted? Let him return home, so that the hearts of his brothers will not melt like his own.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 20:9"
        },
        "When the officers have finished addressing the army, they are to appoint commanders to lead it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 20:10"
        },
        "When you approach a city to fight against it, you are to make an offer of peace. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 20:11"
        },
        "If they accept your offer of peace and open ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their gates"
          ]
        },
        ", all the people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " will become forced laborers to serve you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 20:12"
        },
        "But if they refuse to make peace with you and wage war against you, lay siege to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that city"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 20:13"
        },
        "When the LORD your God has delivered it into your hand, you must put every male to the sword. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 20:14"
        },
        "But the women, children, livestock, and whatever else is in the city— all its spoil— you may take as plunder, and you shall use the spoil of your enemies that the LORD your God gives you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 20:15"
        },
        "This is how you are to treat all the cities that are far away from you and do not belong to the nations nearby."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 20:16"
        },
        "However, in the cities of the nations that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance, you must not leave alive anything that breathes. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 20:17"
        },
        "For you must devote them to complete destruction",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "cherem "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "— the Hittites, Amorites, Canaanites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites— as the LORD your God has commanded you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 20:18"
        },
        "so that they cannot teach you to do all the detestable things they do for their gods, and so cause you to sin against the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 20:19"
        },
        "When you lay siege to a city for an extended time while fighting against it to capture it, you must not destroy its trees by putting an axe to them, because you can eat their fruit. You must not cut them down. Are the trees of the field human, that you should besiege them? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 20:20"
        },
        "But you may destroy the trees that you know do not produce fruit. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Use them"
          ]
        },
        " to build siege works against the city that is waging war against you, until it falls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "21",
      "sid": "DEU 21"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Atonement for an Unsolved Murder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 21:1"
        },
        "If ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " is found slain, lying in a field in the land that the LORD your God is giving you to possess, and it is not known who killed him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 21:2"
        },
        "your elders and judges must come out and measure the distance from the victim to the neighboring cities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 21:3"
        },
        "Then the elders of the city nearest the victim shall take a heifer that has never been yoked or used for work, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 21:4"
        },
        "bring the heifer to a valley with running water that has not been plowed or sown, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and break"
          ]
        },
        " its neck there by the stream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 21:5"
        },
        "And the priests, the sons of Levi, shall come forward, for the LORD your God has chosen them to serve Him and pronounce blessings in His name and to give a ruling in every dispute and case of assault. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 21:6"
        },
        "Then all the elders of the city nearest the victim shall wash their hands by the stream over the heifer whose neck has been broken, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 21:7"
        },
        "and they shall declare, “Our hands did not shed this blood, nor did our eyes see it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 21:8"
        },
        "Accept this atonement, O LORD, for Your people Israel whom You have redeemed, and do not hold the shedding of innocent blood against them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "And the bloodshed will be atoned for. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 21:9"
        },
        "So you shall purge from among you the guilt of shedding innocent blood, since you have done what is right in the eyes of the LORD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Marrying a Captive Woman"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 21:10"
        },
        "When you go to war against your enemies and the LORD your God delivers them into your hand and you take them captive, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 21:11"
        },
        "if you see a beautiful woman among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", and you desire her and want to take her as your wife, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 21:12"
        },
        "then you shall bring her into your house. She must shave her head, trim her nails, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 21:13"
        },
        "and put aside the clothing of her captivity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "After she has lived in your house a full month and mourned her father and mother, you may have relations with her and be her husband, and she shall be your wife. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 21:14"
        },
        "And if you are not pleased with her, you are to let her go wherever she wishes. But you must not sell her for money or treat her as a slave, since you have dishonored her."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Inheritance Rights of the Firstborn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 21:15"
        },
        "If a man has two wives, one beloved and the other unloved, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "both"
          ]
        },
        " bear him sons, but the unloved wife has the firstborn son, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 21:16"
        },
        "when that man assigns his inheritance to his sons he must not appoint the son of the beloved wife as the firstborn over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the son"
          ]
        },
        " of the unloved wife."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 21:17"
        },
        "Instead, he must acknowledge the firstborn, the son of his unloved wife, by giving him a double portion of all that he has. For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that son"
          ]
        },
        " is the firstfruits of his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "father’s"
          ]
        },
        " strength; the right of the firstborn belongs to him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Rebellious Son"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LUK 15:11-32",
          "content": [
            "Luke 15:11–32"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 21:18"
        },
        "If a man has a stubborn and rebellious son who does not obey his father and mother and does not listen to them when disciplined, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 21:19"
        },
        "his father and mother are to lay hold of him and bring him to the elders of his city, to the gate of his hometown, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 21:20"
        },
        "and say to the elders, “This son of ours is stubborn and rebellious; he does not obey us. He is a glutton and a drunkard.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 21:21"
        },
        "Then all the men of his city will stone him to death. So you must purge the evil from among you,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 5:13",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 5:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and all Israel will hear and be afraid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Cursed Is Anyone Hung on a Tree"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 21:22"
        },
        "If a man has committed a sin worthy of death, and he is executed, and you hang his body on a tree,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "impale his body on a pole"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; similarly in verse 23"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 21:23"
        },
        "you must not leave the body on the tree overnight, but you must be sure to bury him that day, because anyone who is hung ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on a tree"
          ]
        },
        " is under God’s curse.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX; Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "anyone who is hanged is under God’s curse"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GAL 3:13",
                  "content": [
                    "Galatians 3:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " You must not defile the land that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "22",
      "sid": "DEU 22"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Various Laws"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 22:1"
        },
        "If you see your brother’s ox or sheep straying, you must not ignore it;",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "you must not hide yourself"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " be sure to return it to your brother. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 22:2"
        },
        "If your brother does not live near you, or if you do not know who he is, you are to take the animal home to remain with you until your brother comes seeking it; then you can return it to him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 22:3"
        },
        "And you shall do the same for his donkey, his cloak, or anything your brother has lost and you have found. You must not ignore it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 22:4"
        },
        "If you see your brother’s donkey or ox fallen on the road, you must not ignore it; you must help him lift it up."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 22:5"
        },
        "A woman must not wear men’s clothing, and a man must not wear women’s clothing, for whoever does these things is detestable to the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 22:6"
        },
        "If you come across a bird’s nest with chicks or eggs, either in a tree or on the ground along the road, and the mother is sitting on the chicks or eggs, you must not take the mother along with the young. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 22:7"
        },
        "You may take the young, but be sure to let the mother go, so that it may be well with you and that you may prolong your days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 22:8"
        },
        "If you build a new house, you are to construct a railing around your roof, so that you do not bring bloodguilt on your house if someone falls from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 22:9"
        },
        "Do not plant your vineyard with two types of seed; if you do, the entire harvest will be defiled",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "will be forfeited to the sanctuary"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " — both the crop you plant and the fruit of your vineyard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 22:10"
        },
        "Do not plow with an ox and a donkey ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "yoked"
          ]
        },
        " together."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 22:11"
        },
        "Do not wear clothes of wool and linen woven together."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 22:12"
        },
        "You are to make tassels on the four corners of the cloak you wear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Marriage Violations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 22:13"
        },
        "Suppose a man marries a woman, has relations with her, and comes to hate her, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 22:14"
        },
        "and he then accuses her of shameful conduct and gives her a bad name, saying, “I married this woman and had relations with her, but I discovered she was not a virgin.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 22:15"
        },
        "Then the young woman’s father and mother shall bring the proof of her virginity to the city elders at the gate ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 22:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " say to the elders, “I gave my daughter in marriage to this man, but he has come to hate her. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 22:17"
        },
        "And now he has accused her of shameful conduct, saying, ‘I discovered that your daughter was not a virgin.’ But here is the proof of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " virginity.” And they shall spread out the cloth before the city elders."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 22:18"
        },
        "Then the elders of that city shall take the man and punish him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 22:19"
        },
        "They are also to fine him a hundred ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "shekels"
          ]
        },
        " of silver",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "100 shekels "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is approximately 2.5 pounds or 1.1 kilograms of silver."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and give them to the young woman’s father, because this man has given a virgin of Israel a bad name. And she shall remain his wife; he must not divorce her as long as he lives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 22:20"
        },
        "If, however, this accusation is true, and no proof of the young woman’s virginity can be found, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 22:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "she"
          ]
        },
        " shall be brought to the door of her father’s house, and there the men of her city will stone her to death. For she has committed an outrage in Israel by being promiscuous in her father’s house. So you must purge the evil from among you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Here and in verse 24; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 5:13",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 5:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 22:22"
        },
        "If a man is found lying with another man’s wife, both the man who slept with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " and the woman must die. You must purge the evil from Israel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 22:23"
        },
        "If there is a virgin pledged in marriage to a man, and another man encounters her in the city and sleeps with her, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 22:24"
        },
        "you must take both of them out to the gate of that city and stone them to death— the young woman because she did not cry out in the city, and the man because he has violated his neighbor’s wife. So you must purge the evil from among you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 22:25"
        },
        "But if the man encounters a betrothed woman in the open country, and he overpowers her and lies with her, only the man who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "has done this"
          ]
        },
        " must die. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 22:26"
        },
        "Do nothing to the young woman, because she ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "has committed"
          ]
        },
        " no sin ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "worthy"
          ]
        },
        " of death. This case is just like one in which a man attacks his neighbor and murders him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 22:27"
        },
        "When he found her in the field, the betrothed woman cried out, but there was no one to save her."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 22:28"
        },
        "If a man encounters a virgin who is not pledged in marriage, and he seizes her and lies with her, and they are discovered, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 22:29"
        },
        "then the man who lay with her must pay the young woman’s father fifty ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "shekels"
          ]
        },
        " of silver,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:29 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "50 shekels "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of silver."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and she must become his wife because he has violated her. He must not divorce her as long as he lives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 22:30"
        },
        "A man is not to marry his father’s wife, so that he will not dishonor his father’s marriage bed.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "uncover his father’s skirt"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "23",
      "sid": "DEU 23"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Exclusion from the Congregation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 23:1"
        },
        "No man with crushed or severed genitals may enter the assembly of the LORD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 23:2"
        },
        "No one of illegitimate birth may enter the assembly of the LORD, nor may any of his descendants, even to the tenth generation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 23:3"
        },
        "No Ammonite or Moabite or any of their descendants may enter the assembly of the LORD, even to the tenth generation. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 23:4"
        },
        "For they did not meet you with food and water on your way out of Egypt, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they hired Balaam son of Beor from Pethor in Aram-naharaim",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mesopotamia; "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Aram-naharaim "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Aram of the two rivers"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", likely the region between the Euphrates and Balih Rivers in northwestern Mesopotamia."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to curse you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 23:5"
        },
        "Yet the LORD your God would not listen to Balaam, and the LORD your God turned the curse into a blessing for you, because the LORD your God loves you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 23:6"
        },
        "You are not to seek peace or prosperity from them as long as you live."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 23:7"
        },
        "Do not despise an Edomite, for he is your brother. Do not despise an Egyptian, because you lived as a foreigner in his land. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 23:8"
        },
        "The third generation of children born to them may enter the assembly of the LORD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Uncleanness in the Camp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 15:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 15:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 23:9"
        },
        "When you are encamped against your enemies, then you shall keep yourself from every wicked thing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 23:10"
        },
        "If any man among you becomes unclean because of a nocturnal emission, he must leave the camp ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " stay outside. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 23:11"
        },
        "When evening approaches, he must wash with water, and when the sun sets he may return to the camp."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 23:12"
        },
        "You must have a place outside the camp to go ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " relieve yourself. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 23:13"
        },
        "And you must have a digging tool in your equipment so that when you relieve yourself you can dig a hole and cover up your excrement."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 23:14"
        },
        "For the LORD your God walks throughout your camp to protect you and deliver your enemies to you. Your camp must be holy, lest He see anything unclean among you and turn away from you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Miscellaneous Laws"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 23:15"
        },
        "Do not return a slave to his master if he has taken refuge with you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 23:16"
        },
        "Let him live among you wherever he chooses, in the town of his pleasing. Do not oppress him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 23:17"
        },
        "No daughter or son of Israel is to be a shrine prostitute. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 23:18"
        },
        "You must not bring the wages of a prostitute, whether female or male,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "or a dog"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " into the house of the LORD your God to fulfill any vow, because both are detestable to the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 23:19"
        },
        "Do not charge your brother interest on money, food, or any other type of loan. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 23:20"
        },
        "You may charge a foreigner interest, but not your brother, so that the LORD your God may bless you in everything to which you put your hand in the land that you are entering to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 23:21"
        },
        "If you make a vow to the LORD your God, do not be slow to keep it, because He will surely require it of you, and you will be guilty of sin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 23:22"
        },
        "But if you refrain from making a vow, you will not be guilty of sin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 23:23"
        },
        "Be careful to follow through on what comes from your lips, because you have freely vowed to the LORD your God with your own mouth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 23:24"
        },
        "When you enter your neighbor’s vineyard, you may eat your fill of grapes, but you must not put any in your basket."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 23:25"
        },
        "When you enter your neighbor’s grainfield, you may pluck the heads of grain with your hand, but you must not put a sickle to your neighbor’s grain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "24",
      "sid": "DEU 24"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Marriage and Divorce Laws"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 5:31-32",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 5:31–32"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LUK 16:18",
          "content": [
            "Luke 16:18"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 24:1"
        },
        "If a man marries a woman, but she becomes displeasing to him because he finds some indecency in her, he may write her a certificate of divorce,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 5:31",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 5:31"
                  ]
                },
                "; see also Mark 10:4."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " hand it to her, and send her away from his house."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 24:2"
        },
        "If, after leaving his house, she goes and becomes another man’s wife, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 24:3"
        },
        "and the second man hates her, writes her a certificate of divorce, hands it to her, and sends her away from his house, or if he dies, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 24:4"
        },
        "then the husband who divorced her first may not remarry her after she has been defiled, for that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " an abomination to the LORD. You must not bring sin upon the land that the LORD your God is giving you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " an inheritance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 24:5"
        },
        "If a man is newly married, he must not be sent to war or be pressed into any duty. For one year he is free to stay at home and bring joy to the wife he has married."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Additional Laws"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 24:6"
        },
        "Do not take a pair of millstones or even an upper millstone as security for a debt, because that would be taking one’s livelihood as security."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 24:7"
        },
        "If a man is caught kidnapping one of his Israelite brothers, whether he treats him as a slave or sells him, the kidnapper must die. So you must purge the evil from among you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 5:13",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 5:13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 24:8"
        },
        "In cases of infectious skin diseases,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Forms of the Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "tzaraath"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", traditionally translated as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "leprosy"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", were used for various skin diseases; see Leviticus 13."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " be careful to diligently follow everything the Levitical priests instruct you. Be careful to do as I have commanded them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 24:9"
        },
        "Remember what the LORD your God did to Miriam on the journey after you came out of Egypt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 24:10"
        },
        "When you lend anything to your neighbor, do not enter his house to collect security. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 24:11"
        },
        "You are to stand outside while the man to whom you are lending brings the security out to you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 24:12"
        },
        "If he is a poor man, you must not go to sleep with the security ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in your possession"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 24:13"
        },
        "be sure to return ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " to him by sunset, so that he may sleep in his own cloak and bless you, and this will be credited to you as righteousness before the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 24:14"
        },
        "Do not oppress a hired hand who is poor and needy, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whether"
          ]
        },
        " he is a brother or a foreigner residing in one of your towns. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 24:15"
        },
        "You are to pay his wages each day before sunset, because he is poor and depends on them. Otherwise he may cry out to the LORD against you, and you will be guilty of sin."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 24:16"
        },
        "Fathers shall not be put to death for their children, nor children for their fathers; each is to die for his own sin.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "2KI 14:6",
                  "content": [
                    "2 Kings 14:6"
                  ]
                },
                " and 2 Chronicles 25:4"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 24:17"
        },
        "Do not deny justice to the foreigner or the fatherless, and do not take a widow’s cloak as security. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 24:18"
        },
        "Remember that you were slaves in Egypt, and the LORD your God redeemed you from that place. Therefore I am commanding you to do this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 24:19"
        },
        "If you are harvesting in your field and forget a sheaf ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ", do not go back to get it. It is to be left for the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow, so that the LORD your God may bless you in all the work of your hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 24:20"
        },
        "When you beat the olives from your trees, you must not go over the branches again. What remains will be for the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 24:21"
        },
        "When you gather the grapes of your vineyard, you must not go over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the vines"
          ]
        },
        " again. What remains will be for the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 24:22"
        },
        "Remember that you were slaves in the land of Egypt. Therefore I am commanding you to do this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "25",
      "sid": "DEU 25"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Fairness and Mercy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 25:1"
        },
        "If there is a dispute between men, they are to go to court to be judged, so that the innocent may be acquitted and the guilty condemned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 25:2"
        },
        "If the guilty man deserves to be beaten, the judge shall have him lie down and be flogged in his presence with the number of lashes his crime warrants. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 25:3"
        },
        "He may receive no more than forty ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "lashes"
          ]
        },
        ", lest your brother be beaten any more than that and be degraded in your sight."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 25:4"
        },
        "Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "25:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1CO 9:9",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Corinthians 9:9"
                  ]
                },
                " and 1 Timothy 5:18"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Widowhood and Marriage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 25:5"
        },
        "When brothers dwell together and one of them dies without a son, the widow must not marry outside ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the family"
          ]
        },
        ". Her husband’s brother is to take her as his wife and fulfill the duty of a brother-in-law for her.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "25:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 22:24",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 22:24"
                  ]
                },
                ", Mark 12:19, and Luke 20:28"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 25:6"
        },
        "The first son she bears will carry on the name of the dead brother, so that his name will not be blotted out from Israel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 25:7"
        },
        "But if the man does not want to marry his brother’s widow, she is to go to the elders at the city gate and say, “My husband’s brother refuses to preserve his brother’s name in Israel. He is not willing to perform the duty of a brother-in-law for me.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 25:8"
        },
        "Then the elders of his city shall summon him and speak with him. If he persists and says, “I do not want to marry her,” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 25:9"
        },
        "his brother’s widow shall go up to him in the presence of the elders, remove his sandal, spit in his face, and declare, “This is what is done to the man who will not maintain his brother’s line.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 25:10"
        },
        "And his family name in Israel will be called “The House of the Unsandaled.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 25:11"
        },
        "If two men are fighting, and the wife of one comes to rescue her husband from the one striking him, and she reaches out her hand and grabs his genitals, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 25:12"
        },
        "you are to cut off her hand. You must show her no pity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Standard Weights and Measures"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PRO 11:1-3",
          "content": [
            "Proverbs 11:1–3"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EZK 45:10-12",
          "content": [
            "Ezekiel 45:10–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 25:13"
        },
        "You shall not have two differing weights in your bag, one heavy and one light. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 25:14"
        },
        "You shall not have two differing measures in your house, one large and one small."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 25:15"
        },
        "You must maintain accurate and honest weights ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " measures, so that you may live long in the land that the LORD your God is giving you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 25:16"
        },
        "For everyone who behaves dishonestly in regard to these things is detestable to the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Revenge on the Amalekites"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 25:17"
        },
        "Remember what the Amalekites did to you along your way from Egypt, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 25:18"
        },
        "how they met you on your journey when you were tired and weary, and they attacked all your stragglers; they had no fear of God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 25:19"
        },
        "When the LORD your God gives you rest from the enemies around you in the land that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " is giving you to possess as an inheritance, you are to blot out the memory of Amalek from under heaven. Do not forget!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "26",
      "sid": "DEU 26"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Offering Firstfruits and Tithes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 27:30-34",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 27:30–34"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 14:22-29",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 14:22–29"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NEH 13:10-14",
          "content": [
            "Nehemiah 13:10–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 26:1"
        },
        "When you enter the land that the LORD your God is giving you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " an inheritance, and you take possession of it and settle in it, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 26:2"
        },
        "you are to take some of the firstfruits of all your produce from the soil of the land that the LORD your God is giving you and put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in a basket. Then go to the place the LORD your God will choose as a dwelling for His Name, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 26:3"
        },
        "to the priest who is serving at that time, and say to him, “I declare today to the LORD your God that I have entered the land that the LORD swore to our fathers to give us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 26:4"
        },
        "Then the priest shall take the basket from your hands and place it before the altar of the LORD your God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 26:5"
        },
        "and you are to declare before the LORD your God, “My father was a wandering Aramean, and he went down to Egypt few in number and lived there and became a great nation, mighty and numerous. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 26:6"
        },
        "But the Egyptians mistreated us and afflicted us, putting us to hard labor. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 26:7"
        },
        "So we called out to the LORD, the God of our fathers; and the LORD heard our voice and saw our affliction, toil, and oppression. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 26:8"
        },
        "Then the LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm, with great terror, signs, and wonders. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 26:9"
        },
        "And He brought us to this place and gave us this land, a land flowing with milk and honey. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 26:10"
        },
        "And now, behold, I have brought the firstfruits of the land that You, O LORD, have given me.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then you are to place ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the basket"
          ]
        },
        " before the LORD your God and bow down before Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 26:11"
        },
        "So you shall rejoice — you, the Levite, and the foreigner dwelling among you — in all the good things the LORD your God has given to you and your household."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 26:12"
        },
        "When you have finished laying aside a tenth of all your produce in the third year, the year of the tithe, you are to give it to the Levite, the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow, that they may eat and be filled within your gates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 26:13"
        },
        "Then you shall declare in the presence of the LORD your God, “I have removed from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " house the sacred ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "portion"
          ]
        },
        " and have given it to the Levite, the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow, according to all the commandments You have given me. I have not transgressed or forgotten Your commandments. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 26:14"
        },
        "I have not eaten any of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the sacred portion"
          ]
        },
        " while in mourning, or removed any of it while unclean, or offered any of it for the dead. I have obeyed the LORD my God; I have done everything You commanded me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 26:15"
        },
        "Look down from Your holy habitation, from heaven, and bless Your people Israel and the land You have given us as You swore to our fathers— a land flowing with milk and honey.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Obey the LORD’s Commands"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 26:16"
        },
        "The LORD your God commands you this day to follow these statutes and ordinances. You must be careful to follow them with all your heart and with all your soul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 26:17"
        },
        "Today you have proclaimed that the LORD is your God and that you will walk in His ways, keep His statutes and commandments and ordinances, and listen to His voice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 26:18"
        },
        "And today the LORD has proclaimed that you are His people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " treasured possession as He promised, that you are to keep all His commandments, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 26:19"
        },
        "that He will set you high in praise and name and honor above all the nations He has made, and that you will be a holy people to the LORD your God, as He has promised."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "27",
      "sid": "DEU 27"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Altar on Mount Ebal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOS 8:30-35",
          "content": [
            "Joshua 8:30–35"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 27:1"
        },
        "Then Moses and the elders of Israel commanded the people: “Keep all the commandments I am giving you today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 27:2"
        },
        "And on the day you cross the Jordan into the land that the LORD your God is giving you, set up large stones and coat them with plaster. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 27:3"
        },
        "Write on them all the words of this law when you have crossed over to enter the land that the LORD your God is giving you, a land flowing with milk and honey, just as the LORD, the God of your fathers, has promised you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 27:4"
        },
        "And when you have crossed the Jordan, you are to set up these stones on Mount Ebal, as I am commanding you today, and you are to coat them with plaster."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 27:5"
        },
        "Moreover, you are to build there an altar to the LORD your God, an altar of stones. You must not use any iron tool on them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 27:6"
        },
        "You shall build the altar of the LORD your God with uncut stones and offer upon it burnt offerings to the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 27:7"
        },
        "There you are to sacrifice ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " peace offerings, eating them and rejoicing in the presence of the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 27:8"
        },
        "And you shall write distinctly upon these stones all the words of this law.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 27:9"
        },
        "Then Moses and the Levitical priests spoke to all Israel: “Be silent, O Israel, and listen! This day you have become the people of the LORD your God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 27:10"
        },
        "You shall therefore obey the voice of the LORD your God and follow His commandments and statutes I am giving you today.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Curses Pronounced from Ebal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 27:11"
        },
        "On that day Moses commanded the people: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 27:12"
        },
        "“When you have crossed the Jordan, these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "tribes"
          ]
        },
        " shall stand on Mount Gerizim to bless the people: Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Joseph, and Benjamin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 27:13"
        },
        "And these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "tribes"
          ]
        },
        " shall stand on Mount Ebal to deliver the curse: Reuben, Gad, Asher, Zebulun, Dan, and Naphtali."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 27:14"
        },
        "Then the Levites shall proclaim in a loud voice to every Israelite:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 27:15"
        },
        "‘Cursed is the man who makes a carved idol or molten image — an abomination to the LORD, the work of the hands of a craftsman — and sets it up in secret.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 27:16"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who dishonors his father or mother.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 27:17"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who moves his neighbor’s boundary stone.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 27:18"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who lets a blind man wander in the road.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 27:19"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who withholds justice from the foreigner, the fatherless, or the widow.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 27:20"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who sleeps with his father’s wife, for he has violated his father’s marriage bed.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "uncovered his father’s skirt"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 27:21"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who lies with any animal.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 27:22"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who sleeps with his sister, the daughter of his father or the daughter of his mother.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 27:23"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who sleeps with his mother-in-law.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 27:24"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who strikes down his neighbor in secret.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 27:25"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who accepts a bribe to kill an innocent person.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "li1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 27:26"
        },
        "‘Cursed is he who does not put the words of this law into practice.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:26 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Cursed is every man who does not continue in all the words of this law"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GAL 3:10",
                  "content": [
                    "Galatians 3:10"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all the people say, ‘Amen!’’’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "28",
      "sid": "DEU 28"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Blessings of Obedience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 25:18-22",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 25:18–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 28:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "“"
          ]
        },
        "Now if you faithfully obey the voice of the LORD your God and are careful to follow all His commandments I am giving you today, the LORD your God will set you high above all the nations of the earth. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 28:2"
        },
        "And all these blessings will come upon you and overtake you, if you will obey the voice of the LORD your God:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 28:3"
        },
        "You will be blessed in the city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and blessed in the country."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 28:4"
        },
        "The fruit of your womb will be blessed,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "as well as the produce of your land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "and the offspring of your livestock —"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the calves of your herds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the lambs of your flocks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 28:5"
        },
        "Your basket and kneading bowl will be blessed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 28:6"
        },
        "You will be blessed when you come in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and blessed when you go out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 28:7"
        },
        "The LORD will cause the enemies who rise up against you to be defeated before you. They will march out against you in one direction but flee from you in seven."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 28:8"
        },
        "The LORD will decree a blessing on your barns and on everything to which you put your hand; the LORD your God will bless you in the land He is giving you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 28:9"
        },
        "The LORD will establish you as His holy people, just as He has sworn to you, if you keep the commandments of the LORD your God and walk in His ways. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 28:10"
        },
        "Then all the peoples of the earth will see that you are called by the name of the LORD, and they will stand in awe of you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 28:11"
        },
        "The LORD will make you prosper abundantly — in the fruit of your womb, the offspring of your livestock, and the produce of your land — in the land that the LORD swore to your fathers to give you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 28:12"
        },
        "The LORD will open the heavens, His abundant storehouse, to send rain on your land in season and to bless all the work of your hands. You will lend to many nations, but borrow from none."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 28:13"
        },
        "The LORD will make you the head and not the tail; you will only move upward and never downward, if you hear and carefully follow the commandments of the LORD your God, which I am giving you today. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 28:14"
        },
        "Do not turn aside to the right or to the left from any of the words I command you today, and do not go after other gods to serve them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Curses of Disobedience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 20:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 20:1–9"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 26:14-39",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 26:14–39"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 28:15"
        },
        "If, however, you do not obey the LORD your God by carefully following all His commandments and statutes I am giving you today, all these curses will come upon you and overtake you:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 28:16"
        },
        "You will be cursed in the city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and cursed in the country."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 28:17"
        },
        "Your basket and kneading bowl will be cursed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 28:18"
        },
        "The fruit of your womb will be cursed,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "as well as the produce of your land,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "the calves of your herds,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the lambs of your flocks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 28:19"
        },
        "You will be cursed when you come in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and cursed when you go out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 28:20"
        },
        "The LORD will send curses upon you, confusion and reproof in all to which you put your hand, until you are destroyed and quickly perish because of the wickedness you have committed in forsaking Him.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Me"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 28:21"
        },
        "The LORD will make the plague cling to you until He has exterminated you from the land that you are entering to possess. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 28:22"
        },
        "The LORD will strike you with wasting disease, with fever and inflammation, with scorching heat and drought,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "sword"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and with blight and mildew; these will pursue you until you perish. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 28:23"
        },
        "The sky over your head will be bronze, and the earth beneath you iron."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 28:24"
        },
        "The LORD will turn the rain of your land into dust and powder; it will descend on you from the sky until you are destroyed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 28:25"
        },
        "The LORD will cause you to be defeated before your enemies. You will march out against them in one direction but flee from them in seven. You will be an object of horror to all the kingdoms of the earth. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 28:26"
        },
        "Your corpses will be food for all the birds of the air and beasts of the earth, with no one to scare them away."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 28:27"
        },
        "The LORD will afflict you with the boils of Egypt, with tumors and scabs and itch from which you cannot be cured."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 28:28"
        },
        "The LORD will afflict you with madness, blindness, and confusion of mind, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 28:29"
        },
        "and at noon you will grope about like a blind man in the darkness. You will not prosper in your ways. Day after day you will be oppressed and plundered, with no one to save you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 28:30"
        },
        "You will be pledged in marriage to a woman, but another man will violate her. You will build a house but will not live in it. You will plant a vineyard but will not enjoy its fruit. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 28:31"
        },
        "Your ox will be slaughtered before your eyes, but you will not eat any of it. Your donkey will be taken away and not returned to you. Your flock will be given to your enemies, and no one will save you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 28:32"
        },
        "Your sons and daughters will be given to another nation, while your eyes grow weary looking for them day after day, with no power in your hand. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "DEU 28:33"
        },
        "A people you do not know will eat the produce of your land and of all your toil. All your days you will be oppressed and crushed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "DEU 28:34"
        },
        "You will be driven mad by the sights you see."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "DEU 28:35"
        },
        "The LORD will afflict you with painful, incurable boils on your knees and thighs, from the soles of your feet to the top of your head."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "DEU 28:36"
        },
        "The LORD will bring you and the king you appoint to a nation neither you nor your fathers have known, and there you will worship other gods— ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "gods"
          ]
        },
        " of wood and stone. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "DEU 28:37"
        },
        "You will become an object of horror, scorn, and ridicule among all the nations to which the LORD will drive you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "DEU 28:38"
        },
        "You will sow much seed in the field but harvest little, because the locusts will consume it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "DEU 28:39"
        },
        "You will plant and cultivate vineyards, but will neither drink the wine nor gather ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the grapes"
          ]
        },
        ", because worms will eat them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "DEU 28:40"
        },
        "You will have olive trees throughout your territory but will never anoint yourself with oil, because the olives will drop off. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "DEU 28:41"
        },
        "You will father sons and daughters, but they will not remain yours, because they will go into captivity. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "DEU 28:42"
        },
        "Swarms of locusts will consume all your trees and the produce of your land."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "DEU 28:43"
        },
        "The foreigner living among you will rise higher and higher above you, while you sink down lower and lower. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "DEU 28:44"
        },
        "He will lend to you, but you will not lend to him. He will be the head, and you will be the tail."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "DEU 28:45"
        },
        "All these curses will come upon you. They will pursue you and overtake you until you are destroyed, since you did not obey the LORD your God and keep the commandments and statutes He gave you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "DEU 28:46"
        },
        "These curses will be a sign and a wonder upon you and your descendants forever."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "DEU 28:47"
        },
        "Because you did not serve the LORD your God with joy and gladness of heart in all your abundance, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "DEU 28:48"
        },
        "you will serve your enemies the LORD will send against you in famine, thirst, nakedness, and destitution. He will place an iron yoke on your neck until He has destroyed you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "DEU 28:49"
        },
        "The LORD will bring a nation from afar, from the ends of the earth, to swoop down upon you like an eagle — a nation whose language you will not understand, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "DEU 28:50"
        },
        "a ruthless nation with no respect for the old and no pity for the young. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "DEU 28:51"
        },
        "They will eat the offspring of your livestock and the produce of your land until you are destroyed. They will leave you no grain or new wine or oil, no calves of your herds or lambs of your flocks, until they have caused you to perish. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "DEU 28:52"
        },
        "They will besiege all the cities throughout your land, until the high and fortified walls in which you trust have fallen. They will besiege all your cities throughout the land that the LORD your God has given you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "DEU 28:53"
        },
        "Then you will eat the fruit of your womb, the flesh of the sons and daughters whom the LORD your God has given you, in the siege and distress that your enemy will inflict on you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "DEU 28:54"
        },
        "The most gentle and refined man among you will begrudge his brother, the wife he embraces,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:54 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the wife of his bosom"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and the rest of his children who have survived, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "DEU 28:55"
        },
        "refusing to share with any of them the flesh of his children he will eat because he has nothing left in the siege and distress that your enemy will inflict on you within all your gates.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:55 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "within all your cities"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; similarly in verse 57"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "DEU 28:56"
        },
        "The most gentle and refined woman among you, so gentle and refined she would not venture to set the sole of her foot on the ground, will begrudge the husband she embraces",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:56 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the husband of her bosom"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and her son and daughter ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "57",
          "sid": "DEU 28:57"
        },
        "the afterbirth that comes from between her legs and the children she bears, because she will secretly eat them for lack of anything else in the siege and distress that your enemy will inflict on you within your gates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "58",
          "sid": "DEU 28:58"
        },
        "If you are not careful to observe all the words of this law which are written in this book, that you may fear this glorious and awesome name— the LORD your God— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "59",
          "sid": "DEU 28:59"
        },
        "He ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will bring"
          ]
        },
        " upon you and your descendants extraordinary disasters, severe and lasting plagues, and terrible and chronic sicknesses. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "60",
          "sid": "DEU 28:60"
        },
        "He will afflict you again with all the diseases you dreaded in Egypt, and they will cling to you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "61",
          "sid": "DEU 28:61"
        },
        "The LORD will also bring upon you every sickness and plague not recorded in this Book of the Law, until you are destroyed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "62",
          "sid": "DEU 28:62"
        },
        "You who were as numerous as the stars in the sky will be left few in number, because you would not obey the voice of the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "63",
          "sid": "DEU 28:63"
        },
        "Just as it pleased the LORD to make you prosper and multiply, so also it will please Him to annihilate you and destroy you. And you will be uprooted from the land you are entering to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "64",
          "sid": "DEU 28:64"
        },
        "Then the LORD will scatter you among all the nations, from one end of the earth to the other, and there you will worship other gods, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "gods"
          ]
        },
        " of wood and stone, which neither you nor your fathers have known. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "65",
          "sid": "DEU 28:65"
        },
        "Among those nations you will find no repose, not even a resting place for the sole of your foot. There the LORD will give you a trembling heart, failing eyes, and a despairing soul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "66",
          "sid": "DEU 28:66"
        },
        "So your life will hang in doubt before you, and you will be afraid night and day, never certain of survival. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "67",
          "sid": "DEU 28:67"
        },
        "In the morning you will say, ‘If only it were evening!’ and in the evening you will say, ‘If only it were morning!’— because of the dread in your hearts of the terrifying sights you will see."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "68",
          "sid": "DEU 28:68"
        },
        "The LORD will return you to Egypt in ships by a route that I said you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "should"
          ]
        },
        " never see again. There you will sell yourselves to your enemies as male and female slaves, but no one will buy you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "29",
      "sid": "DEU 29"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Covenant in Moab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 29:1"
        },
        "These are the words of the covenant that the LORD commanded Moses to make with the Israelites in the land of Moab, in addition to the covenant He had made with them at Horeb.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "29:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 29:2"
        },
        "Moses summoned all Israel and proclaimed to them, “You have seen with your own eyes everything the LORD did in Egypt to Pharaoh, to all his officials, and to all his land. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 29:3"
        },
        "You saw with your own eyes the great trials, and those miraculous signs and wonders. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 29:4"
        },
        "Yet to this day the LORD has not given you a mind to understand, eyes to see, or ears to hear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 29:5"
        },
        "For forty years I led you in the wilderness,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "yet your clothes and sandals did not wear out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 29:6"
        },
        "You ate no bread and drank ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "no"
          ]
        },
        " wine or strong drink,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "so that you might know that I am the LORD your God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 29:7"
        },
        "When you reached this place, Sihon king of Heshbon and Og king of Bashan came out against us in battle, but we defeated them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 29:8"
        },
        "We took their land and gave it as an inheritance to the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 29:9"
        },
        "So keep and follow the words of this covenant, that you may prosper in all you do."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 29:10"
        },
        "All of you are standing today before the LORD your God— you leaders of tribes,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "29:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX and Syriac; Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "you leaders, tribes"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " elders, officials, and all the men of Israel, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 29:11"
        },
        "your children and wives, and the foreigners in your camps who cut your wood and draw your water— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 29:12"
        },
        "so that you may enter into the covenant of the LORD your God, which He is making with you today, and into His oath, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 29:13"
        },
        "and so that He may establish you today as His people, and He may be your God as He promised you and as He swore to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 29:14"
        },
        "I am making this covenant and this oath not only with you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 29:15"
        },
        "but also with those who are standing here with us today in the presence of the LORD our God, as well as with those who are not here today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 29:16"
        },
        "For you yourselves know how we lived in the land of Egypt and how we passed through the nations on the way ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 29:17"
        },
        "You saw the abominations and idols among them made of wood and stone, of silver and gold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 29:18"
        },
        "Make sure there is no man or woman, clan or tribe among you today whose heart turns away from the LORD our God to go and worship the gods of those nations. Make sure there is no root among you that bears such poisonous and bitter fruit,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "29:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 12:15",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 12:15"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 29:19"
        },
        "because when such a person hears the words of this oath,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "29:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "curse"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " he invokes a blessing on himself, saying, ‘I will have peace, even though I walk in the stubbornness of my own heart.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "This will bring disaster on the watered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "land"
          ]
        },
        " as well as the dry. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 29:20"
        },
        "The LORD will never be willing to forgive him. Instead, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " anger and jealousy will burn against that man, and every curse written in this book will fall upon him. The LORD will blot out his name from under heaven ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 29:21"
        },
        "and single him out from all the tribes of Israel for disaster, according to all the curses of the covenant written in this Book of the Law."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 29:22"
        },
        "Then the generation to come — your sons who follow you and the foreigner who comes from a distant land — will see the plagues of the land and the sicknesses the LORD has inflicted on it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 29:23"
        },
        "All its soil will be a burning waste of sulfur and salt, unsown and unproductive, with no plant growing on it, just like the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah, Admah and Zeboiim, which the LORD overthrew in His fierce anger."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 29:24"
        },
        "So all the nations will ask, ‘Why has the LORD done such a thing to this land? Why this great outburst of anger?’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 29:25"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " will answer, ‘It is because they abandoned the covenant of the LORD, the God of their fathers, which He made with them when He brought them out of the land of Egypt. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 29:26"
        },
        "They went and served other gods, and they worshiped gods they had not known— gods that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the LORD"
          ]
        },
        " had not given to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 29:27"
        },
        "Therefore the anger of the LORD burned against this land, and He brought upon it every curse written in this book. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 29:28"
        },
        "The LORD uprooted them from their land in His anger, rage, and great wrath, and He cast them into another land, where they are today.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 29:29"
        },
        "The secret ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "things belong"
          ]
        },
        " to the LORD our God, but the things revealed belong to us and to our children forever, so that we may follow all the words of this law.’’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "30",
      "sid": "DEU 30"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Promise of Restoration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NEH 1:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Nehemiah 1:1–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 30:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "“"
          ]
        },
        "When all these things come upon you— the blessings and curses I have set before you— and you call ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " to mind in all the nations to which the LORD your God has banished you, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 30:2"
        },
        "and when you and your children return to the LORD your God and obey His voice with all your heart and all your soul according to everything I am giving you today, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 30:3"
        },
        "then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " will restore you from captivity",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "30:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "restore your fortunes"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and have compassion on you and gather you from all the nations to which the LORD your God has scattered you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 30:4"
        },
        "Even if you have been banished to the farthest horizon,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "30:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to the extremity of the heavens"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He will gather you and return you from there.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "30:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "NEH 1:8-9",
                  "content": [
                    "Nehemiah 1:8–9"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 30:5"
        },
        "And the LORD your God will bring you into the land your fathers possessed, and you will take possession of it. He will cause you to prosper and multiply more than your fathers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 30:6"
        },
        "The LORD your God will circumcise your hearts and the hearts of your descendants, and you will love Him with all your heart and with all your soul, so that you may live."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 30:7"
        },
        "Then the LORD your God will put all these curses upon your enemies who hate you and persecute you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 30:8"
        },
        "And you will again obey the voice of the LORD and follow all His commandments I am giving you today. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 30:9"
        },
        "So the LORD your God will make you abound in all the work of your hands ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " in the fruit of your womb, the offspring of your livestock, and the produce of your land. Indeed, the LORD will again delight in your prosperity, as He delighted in that of your fathers, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 30:10"
        },
        "if you obey the LORD your God by keeping His commandments and statutes that are written in this Book of the Law, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " if you turn to Him with all your heart and with all your soul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Choice of Life or Death"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 30:11"
        },
        "For this commandment I give you today is not too difficult for you or beyond your reach. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 30:12"
        },
        "It is not in heaven, that you should need to ask, ‘Who will ascend into heaven",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "30:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 10:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 10:6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to get it for us and proclaim it, that we may obey it?’ ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 30:13"
        },
        "And it is not beyond the sea, that you should need to ask, ‘Who will cross the sea",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "30:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 10:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 10:7"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to get it for us and proclaim it, that we may obey it?’ ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 30:14"
        },
        "But the word ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " very near you; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " in your mouth and in your heart,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "30:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 10:8",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 10:8"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " so that you may obey it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 30:15"
        },
        "See, I have set before you today life and prosperity, as well as death and disaster. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 30:16"
        },
        "For I am commanding you today to love the LORD your God, to walk in His ways, and to keep His commandments, statutes, and ordinances, so that you may live and increase, and the LORD your God may bless you in the land that you are entering to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 30:17"
        },
        "But if your heart turns away and you do not listen, but are drawn away to bow down to other gods and worship them, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 30:18"
        },
        "I declare to you today that you will surely perish; you shall not prolong ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " days in the land that you are crossing the Jordan to possess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 30:19"
        },
        "I call heaven and earth as witnesses against you today that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing. Therefore choose life, so that you and your descendants may live, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 30:20"
        },
        "and that you may love the LORD your God, obey Him, and hold fast to Him. For He ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " your life, and He will prolong your life in the land that the LORD swore to give to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "31",
      "sid": "DEU 31"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Joshua to Succeed Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 27:18-23",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 27:18–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 31:1"
        },
        "When Moses had finished speaking",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "31:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "DSS and LXX; MT "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "When Moses went out and spoke"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " these words to all Israel, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 31:2"
        },
        "he said to them, “I am now a hundred and twenty years old; I am no longer able to come and go, and the LORD has said to me, ‘You shall not cross the Jordan.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 31:3"
        },
        "The LORD your God Himself will cross over ahead of you. He will destroy these nations before you, and you will dispossess them. Joshua will cross ahead of you, as the LORD has said. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 31:4"
        },
        "And the LORD will do to them as He did to Sihon and Og, the kings of the Amorites, when He destroyed them along with their land."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 31:5"
        },
        "The LORD will deliver them over to you, and you must do to them exactly as I have commanded you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 31:6"
        },
        "Be strong and courageous; do not be afraid or terrified of them, for it is the LORD your God who goes with you; He will never leave you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "nor"
          ]
        },
        " forsake you.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "31:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 13:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 13:5"
                  ]
                },
                "; here and in verse 8"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 31:7"
        },
        "Then Moses called for Joshua and said to him in the presence of all Israel, “Be strong and courageous, for you will go with this people into the land that the LORD swore to their fathers to give them, and you shall give it to them as an inheritance. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 31:8"
        },
        "The LORD Himself goes before you; He will be with you. He will never leave you nor forsake you. Do not be afraid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " discouraged.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Reading of the Law"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NEH 8:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Nehemiah 8:1–8"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 31:9"
        },
        "So Moses wrote down this law and gave it to the priests, the sons of Levi, who carried the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and to all the elders of Israel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 31:10"
        },
        "Then Moses commanded them, “At the end of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "every"
          ]
        },
        " seven years, at the appointed time in the year of remission ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of debt"
          ]
        },
        ", during the Feast of Tabernacles,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "31:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Booths "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Shelters "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "and originally called "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Ingathering"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 23:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 23:16"
                  ]
                },
                " and Exodus 34:22)."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 31:11"
        },
        "when all Israel comes before the LORD your God at the place He will choose, you are to read this law in the hearing of all Israel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 31:12"
        },
        "Assemble the people— men, women, children, and the foreigners within your gates— so that they may listen and learn to fear the LORD your God and to follow carefully all the words of this law. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 31:13"
        },
        "Then their children who do not know ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the law"
          ]
        },
        " will listen and learn to fear the LORD your God, as long as you live in the land that you are crossing the Jordan to possess.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "God Commissions Joshua"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 31:14"
        },
        "Then the LORD said to Moses, “Behold, the time of your death is near. Call Joshua and present yourselves at the Tent of Meeting, so that I may commission him.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "So Moses and Joshua went and presented themselves at the Tent of Meeting. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 31:15"
        },
        "Then the LORD appeared at the tent in a pillar of cloud, and the cloud stood over the entrance to the tent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 31:16"
        },
        "And the LORD said to Moses, “You will soon rest with your fathers, and these people will rise up and prostitute themselves with the foreign gods of the land they are entering. They will forsake Me and break the covenant I have made with them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 31:17"
        },
        "On that day My anger will burn against them, and I will abandon them and hide My face from them, so that they will be consumed, and many troubles and afflictions will befall them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "On that day they will say, ‘Have not these disasters come upon us because our God is no longer with us?’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 31:18"
        },
        "And on that day I will surely hide My face because of all the evil they have done by turning to other gods."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 31:19"
        },
        "Now therefore, write down for yourselves this song and teach it to the Israelites; have them recite it, so that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " may be a witness for Me against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 31:20"
        },
        "When I have brought them into the land that I swore to give their fathers, a land flowing with milk and honey, they will eat their fill and prosper. Then they will turn to other gods and worship them, and they will reject Me and break My covenant. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 31:21"
        },
        "And when many troubles and afflictions have come upon them, this song will testify against them, because it will not be forgotten from the lips of their descendants. For I know their inclination, even before I bring them into the land that I swore to give them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 31:22"
        },
        "So that very day Moses wrote down this song and taught it to the Israelites."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 31:23"
        },
        "Then the LORD commissioned Joshua son of Nun and said, “Be strong and courageous, for you will bring the Israelites into the land that I swore to give them, and I will be with you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Law Placed in the Ark"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 31:24"
        },
        "When Moses had finished writing in a book the words of this law from beginning to end, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 31:25"
        },
        "he gave this command to the Levites who carried the ark of the covenant of the LORD: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 31:26"
        },
        "“Take this Book of the Law and place it beside the ark of the covenant of the LORD your God, so that it may remain there as a witness against you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 31:27"
        },
        "For I know how rebellious and stiff-necked you are. If you are already rebelling against the LORD while I am still alive, how much more will you rebel after my death!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 31:28"
        },
        "Assemble before me all the elders of your tribes and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " your officers so that I may speak these words in their hearing and call heaven and earth to witness against them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 31:29"
        },
        "For I know that after my death you will become utterly corrupt and turn from the path I have commanded you. And in the days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to come"
          ]
        },
        ", disaster will befall you because you will do evil in the sight of the LORD to provoke Him to anger by the work of your hands.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Moses Begins His Song"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 31:30"
        },
        "Then Moses recited aloud to the whole assembly of Israel the words of this song ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from beginning"
          ]
        },
        " to end:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "32",
      "sid": "DEU 32"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Song of Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "REV 15:1-4",
          "content": [
            "Revelation 15:1–4"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 32:1"
        },
        "Give ear, O heavens, and I will speak;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "hear, O earth, the words of my mouth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 32:2"
        },
        "Let my teaching fall like rain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and my speech settle like dew,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "like gentle rain on new grass,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "like showers on tender plants."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 32:3"
        },
        "For I will proclaim the name of the LORD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "Ascribe greatness to our God!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 32:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He is"
          ]
        },
        " the Rock, His work is perfect;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "all His ways are just."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "A God of faithfulness without injustice,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "righteous and upright ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " He."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 32:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His people"
          ]
        },
        " have acted corruptly toward Him;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the blemish ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on them is"
          ]
        },
        " not that of His children,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "but of a perverse and crooked generation.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PHP 2:15",
                  "content": [
                    "Philippians 2:15"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 32:6"
        },
        "Is this how you repay the LORD,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "O foolish and senseless people?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Is He not your Father and Creator?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "Has He not made you and established you?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 32:7"
        },
        "Remember the days of old;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "consider the years long past."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Ask your father, and he will tell you,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "your elders, and they will inform you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 32:8"
        },
        "When the Most High gave the nations their inheritance,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "when He divided the sons of man,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He set the boundaries of the peoples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "according to the number of the sons of God.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "DSS; LXX "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "according to the number of the angels of God"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; MT "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "according to the number of the sons of Israel"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 32:9"
        },
        "But the LORD’s portion is His people,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "Jacob His allotted inheritance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 32:10"
        },
        "He found him in a desert land,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "in a barren, howling wilderness;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He surrounded him, He instructed him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "He guarded him as the apple",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the pupil"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of His eye."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 32:11"
        },
        "As an eagle stirs up its nest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and hovers over its young,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He spread His wings to catch them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " carried them on His pinions.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Pinions "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "are the outer parts of a bird’s wings, including the flight feathers."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 32:12"
        },
        "The LORD alone led him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and no foreign god ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " with him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 32:13"
        },
        "He made him ride on the heights of the land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and fed him the produce of the field."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He nourished him with honey from the rock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and oil from the flinty crag,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 32:14"
        },
        "with curds from the herd and milk from the flock,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with the fat of lambs,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "with rams from Bashan, and goats,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with the choicest grains of wheat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "From the juice of the finest grapes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "you drank the wine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 32:15"
        },
        "But Jeshurun",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Jeshurun "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the upright one"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", a term of endearment for Israel."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " grew fat and kicked—"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "becoming fat, bloated, and gorged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He abandoned the God who made him"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and scorned the Rock of his salvation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 32:16"
        },
        "They provoked His jealousy with foreign gods;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "they enraged Him with abominations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 32:17"
        },
        "They sacrificed to demons, not to God,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to gods they had not known,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "to newly arrived ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "gods"
          ]
        },
        ","
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "which your fathers did not fear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 32:18"
        },
        "You ignored the Rock who brought you forth;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "you forgot the God who gave you birth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 32:19"
        },
        "When the LORD saw this, He rejected ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ","
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "provoked to anger by His sons and daughters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 32:20"
        },
        "He said: “I will hide My face from them;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will see what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will be"
          ]
        },
        " their end."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "For they are a perverse generation—"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "children of unfaithfulness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 32:21"
        },
        "They have provoked My jealousy by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that which is"
          ]
        },
        " not God;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "they have enraged Me with their worthless idols."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "So I will make them jealous by those who are not a people;",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "not a nation"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see also LXX."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will make them angry by a nation without understanding.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 10:19",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 10:19"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 32:22"
        },
        "For a fire has been kindled by My anger,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and it burns to the depths of Sheol;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "it consumes the earth and its produce,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and scorches the foundations of the mountains."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 32:23"
        },
        "I will heap disasters upon them;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will spend My arrows against them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 32:24"
        },
        "They will be wasted from hunger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and ravaged by pestilence and bitter plague;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "I will send the fangs of wild beasts against them,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with the venom of vipers that slither in the dust."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 32:25"
        },
        "Outside, the sword will take their children,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and inside, terror will strike"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "the young man and the young woman,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the infant and the gray-haired man."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 32:26"
        },
        "I would have said that I would cut them to pieces"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and blot out their memory from mankind,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 32:27"
        },
        "if I had not dreaded the taunt of the enemy,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "lest their adversaries misunderstand and say:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘Our own hand has prevailed;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "it was not the LORD who did all this.’”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 32:28"
        },
        "Israel is a nation devoid of counsel,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with no understanding among them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 32:29"
        },
        "If only they were wise, they would understand it;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "they would comprehend their fate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "DEU 32:30"
        },
        "How could one man pursue a thousand,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "or two put ten thousand to flight,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "unless their Rock had sold them,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "unless the LORD had given them up?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "DEU 32:31"
        },
        "For their rock is not like our Rock,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "even our enemies concede.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:31 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew; LXX "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "but our enemies are void of understanding"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "DEU 32:32"
        },
        "But their vine ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " from the vine of Sodom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and from the fields of Gomorrah."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Their grapes are poisonous;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "their clusters ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " bitter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "DEU 32:33"
        },
        "Their wine is the venom of serpents,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the deadly poison of cobras."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "DEU 32:34"
        },
        "“Have I not stored up these things,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "sealed up within My vaults?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "DEU 32:35"
        },
        "Vengeance is Mine; I will repay.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX; Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Vengeance is Mine, and recompense"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 12:19",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 12:19"
                  ]
                },
                " and Hebrews 10:30"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "In due time their foot will slip;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "for their day of disaster is near,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and their doom is coming quickly.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "DEU 32:36"
        },
        "For the LORD will vindicate His people",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:36 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "will judge His people"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see also LXX; cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 10:30",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 10:30"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and have compassion on His servants"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "when He sees that their strength is gone"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and no one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "remains"
          ]
        },
        ", slave or free."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "DEU 32:37"
        },
        "He will say: “Where are their gods,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the rock in which they took refuge,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "DEU 32:38"
        },
        "which ate the fat of their sacrifices"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and drank the wine of their drink offerings?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Let them rise up and help you;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "let them give you shelter!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "DEU 32:39"
        },
        "See now that I am He;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "there is no God besides Me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "I bring death and I give life;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I wound and I heal,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there is"
          ]
        },
        " no one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "who can deliver from My hand."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "DEU 32:40"
        },
        "For I lift up My hand to heaven and declare:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "As surely as I live forever,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "DEU 32:41"
        },
        "when I sharpen My flashing sword,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and My hand grasps it in judgment,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "I will take vengeance on My adversaries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and repay those who hate Me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "DEU 32:42"
        },
        "I will make My arrows drunk with blood,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "while My sword devours flesh—"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "the blood of the slain and captives,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the heads of the enemy leaders.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "DEU 32:43"
        },
        "Rejoice, [O heavens, with Him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and let all God’s angels worship Him.]",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See DSS and LXX; MT lacks "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Rejoice, O heavens, with Him, and let all God’s angels worship Him."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 1:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 1:6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Rejoice,"
          ]
        },
        " O nations, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " His people;",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ROM 15:10",
                  "content": [
                    "Romans 15:10"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "for He will avenge the blood of His children.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "DSS and LXX; MT "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "servants"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He will take vengeance on His adversaries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "[and repay those who hate Him];",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX and Vulgate; MT lacks "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and repay those who hate Him"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He will cleanse His land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " His people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "DEU 32:44"
        },
        "Then Moses came with Joshua",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "32:44 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Hoshea"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", a variant of "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Joshua"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " son of Nun and recited all the words of this song in the hearing of the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "DEU 32:45"
        },
        "When Moses had finished reciting all these words to all Israel, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "DEU 32:46"
        },
        "he said to them, “Take to heart all the words I have solemnly declared to you this day, so that you may command your children to carefully follow all the words of this law. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "DEU 32:47"
        },
        "For they are not idle words to you, because they are your life, and by them you will live long in the land that you are crossing the Jordan to possess.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Moses’ Death Foretold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "DEU 32:48"
        },
        "On that same day the LORD said to Moses, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "DEU 32:49"
        },
        "“Go up into the Abarim Range to Mount Nebo, in the land of Moab across from Jericho, and view the land of Canaan, which I am giving to the Israelites as their own possession."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "DEU 32:50"
        },
        "And there on the mountain that you climb, you will die and be gathered to your people, just as your brother Aaron died on Mount Hor and was gathered to his people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "DEU 32:51"
        },
        "For at the waters of Meribah-kadesh in the Wilderness of Zin, both of you broke faith with Me among the Israelites by failing to treat Me as holy in their presence. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "DEU 32:52"
        },
        "Although you shall see from a distance the land that I am giving the Israelites, you shall not enter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "33",
      "sid": "DEU 33"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Moses Blesses the Twelve Tribes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 33:1"
        },
        "This is the blessing that Moses the man of God pronounced upon the Israelites before his death. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 33:2"
        },
        "He said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“The LORD came from Sinai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and dawned upon us",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "upon them"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " from Seir;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He shone forth from Mount Paran"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and came with myriads of holy ones,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with flaming fire at His right hand.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "with myriads of holy ones from the south, from His mountain slopes"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 33:3"
        },
        "Surely You love the people;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "all the holy ones ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " in Your hand,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "and they sit down at Your feet;",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they follow in Your steps"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "each receives Your words —"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 33:4"
        },
        "the law that Moses gave us,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the possession of the assembly of Jacob."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 33:5"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the LORD"
          ]
        },
        " became King in Jeshurun",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Jeshurun "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the upright one"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", a term of endearment for Israel; also in verse 26."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "when the leaders of the people gathered,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "when the tribes of Israel ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "came"
          ]
        },
        " together."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 33:6"
        },
        "Let Reuben live and not die,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "nor",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "but let"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " his men be few.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 33:7"
        },
        "And concerning Judah he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“O LORD, hear the cry of Judah"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and bring him to his people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "With his own hands he defends his cause,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "but may You be a help against his foes.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 33:8"
        },
        "Concerning Levi he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Give"
          ]
        },
        " Your Thummim ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Levi"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and Your Urim to Your godly one,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "DSS and LXX; MT does not include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to Levi"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Let Your Perfections and Your Lights be to Your godly one"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "whom You tested at Massah",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Massah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "testing"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 17:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 17:7"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and contested at the waters of Meribah.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Meribah "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "means "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "quarreling"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 17:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 17:7"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 33:9"
        },
        "He said of his father and mother,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "‘I do not consider them.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He disregarded his brothers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and did not know his own sons,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "for he kept",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they kept"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", most likely referring to Levi in the plural; similarly twice in verse 10"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Your word"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and maintained Your covenant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 33:10"
        },
        "He will teach Your ordinances to Jacob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and Your law to Israel;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "he will set incense before You"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and whole burnt offerings on Your altar."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 33:11"
        },
        "Bless his substance, O LORD,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and accept the work of his hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Smash the loins of those who rise against him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and of his foes so they can rise ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "no more"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 33:12"
        },
        "Concerning Benjamin he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“May the beloved of the LORD"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "rest secure in Him;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " shields",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "LXX; Hebrew "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "He shields"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " him all day long,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and upon His shoulders he rests.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "DEU 33:13"
        },
        "Concerning Joseph he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“May his land be blessed by the LORD"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with the precious dew from heaven above"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the deep waters that lie beneath,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "DEU 33:14"
        },
        "with the bountiful harvest from the sun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the abundant yield of the seasons,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "DEU 33:15"
        },
        "with the best of the ancient mountains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the bounty of the everlasting hills,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "DEU 33:16"
        },
        "with the choice gifts of the land and everything in it,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and with the favor of Him who dwelt in the burning bush."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "May these rest on the head of Joseph"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and crown the brow of the prince of his brothers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "DEU 33:17"
        },
        "His majesty ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is like"
          ]
        },
        " a firstborn bull,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and his horns are like those of a wild ox."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "With them he will gore the nations,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "even to the ends of the earth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Such are the myriads of Ephraim,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and such are the thousands of Manasseh.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "DEU 33:18"
        },
        "Concerning Zebulun he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Rejoice, Zebulun, in your journeys,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and Issachar, in your tents."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "DEU 33:19"
        },
        "They will call the peoples to a mountain;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "there they will offer sacrifices of righteousness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "For they will feast on the abundance of the seas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the hidden treasures of the sand.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "DEU 33:20"
        },
        "Concerning Gad he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Blessed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " he who enlarges"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the domain of"
          ]
        },
        " Gad!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He lies down like a lion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and tears off an arm or a head."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "DEU 33:21"
        },
        "He chose the best ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "land"
          ]
        },
        " for himself,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "because a ruler’s portion was reserved for him there."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He came with the leaders of the people;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "he administered the LORD’s justice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and His ordinances for Israel.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "DEU 33:22"
        },
        "Concerning Dan he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Dan ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a lion’s cub,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "leaping out of Bashan.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "DEU 33:23"
        },
        "Concerning Naphtali he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Naphtali is abounding with favor,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "full of the blessing of the LORD;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "he shall take possession"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "of the sea",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "33:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the west"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and the south.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "DEU 33:24"
        },
        "And concerning Asher he said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“May Asher be the most blessed of sons;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "may he be the most favored among his brothers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and dip his foot in oil."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "DEU 33:25"
        },
        "May the bolts of your gate be iron and bronze,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and may your strength match your days.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "DEU 33:26"
        },
        "“There is none like the God of Jeshurun,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "who rides the heavens to your aid,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the clouds in His majesty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "DEU 33:27"
        },
        "The eternal God is your dwelling place,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and underneath are the everlasting arms."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He drives out the enemy before you,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "giving the command, ‘Destroy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        "!’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "DEU 33:28"
        },
        "So Israel dwells securely;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the fountain of Jacob lives untroubled"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "in a land of grain and new wine,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "where even the heavens drip with dew."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "DEU 33:29"
        },
        "Blessed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " you, O Israel!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "Who is like you, a people saved by the LORD?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "He is the shield that protects you,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the sword in which you boast."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Your enemies will cower before you,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and you shall trample their high places.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "34",
      "sid": "DEU 34"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Death of Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "DEU 34:1"
        },
        "Then Moses went up from the plains of Moab to Mount Nebo, to the top of Pisgah, which faces Jericho. And the LORD showed him the whole land — from Gilead as far as Dan, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "DEU 34:2"
        },
        "all of Naphtali, the land of Ephraim and Manasseh, all the land of Judah as far as the Western Sea,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "34:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "DEU 34:3"
        },
        "the Negev, and the region from the Valley of Jericho (the City of Palms) all the way to Zoar."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "DEU 34:4"
        },
        "And the LORD said to him, “This is the land that I swore to give Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob when I said, ‘I will give it to your descendants.’ I have let you see it with your own eyes, but you will not cross into it.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "DEU 34:5"
        },
        "So Moses the servant of the LORD died there in the land of Moab, as the LORD had said. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "DEU 34:6"
        },
        "And He buried him",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "34:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "SP and some LXX manuscripts "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they buried him"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " in a valley in the land of Moab facing Beth-peor, and no one to this day knows the location of his grave."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "DEU 34:7"
        },
        "Moses ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " a hundred and twenty years old when he died, yet his eyes were not weak, and his vitality had not diminished. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "DEU 34:8"
        },
        "The Israelites grieved for Moses in the plains of Moab thirty days, until the time of weeping and mourning for Moses came to an end."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "DEU 34:9"
        },
        "Now Joshua son of Nun was filled with the spirit of wisdom because Moses had laid his hands on him. So the Israelites obeyed him and did as the LORD had commanded Moses. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "DEU 34:10"
        },
        "Since that time, no prophet has risen in Israel like Moses, whom the LORD knew face to face— ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "DEU 34:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "no prophet who did"
          ]
        },
        " all the signs and wonders that the LORD sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses"
          ]
        },
        " to do in the land of Egypt to Pharaoh and to all his officials and all his land, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "DEU 34:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and no prophet who"
          ]
        },
        " performed all the mighty acts of power and awesome deeds",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "34:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "terrifying deeds"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " that Moses ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " in the sight of all Israel."
      ]
    }
  ]
}